select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'fleet-and-listings', 'chapter', 'calendar-sync-with-turo-and-other-platforms', 'Vehicles is the fleet. Listings turns a car into a page on carmacars.ca in four steps: photos, covered plates, a review, and live on the site.

## Vehicles

**Cars** > **Vehicles**

1. Filter by status; More filters has who supplies the car, retired cars and the mode. Each row shows the plate, class, owner, mode, status, listing and daily rate.
2. Search by plate, model or owner. **Cars** > **Rates for many cars** changes the rates of many cars at once.
3. Open a car for its tabs: Overview, Rates, Fees and coverage, Calendar, Listing, and Owner, documents, tracker. The Tracker card links to Fleet tracking.

![](/guides/img/admin-08-vehicles-desktop-46461f49.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 900; address: carmacars.ca/admin/vehicles; pins: 1 74.3 31.1, 2 37.5 24.3, 3 48.6 52.4")

## Set a car''s rates and kilometres

Open the car, then the **Rates** tab. Everything on it saves together, in one step.

1. Type the four rates. Only the daily rate is needed: an empty weekend rate is the daily rate, an empty weekly rate is 6 days at the daily rate, and an empty monthly rate is 22 days.
2. Kilometres: keep **Use the defaults** (the kilometres a day in Settings, Kilometre choices, and the extra kilometre rate in Fee defaults for the car''s class), or choose **Custom for this car** and type them.
3. Check the deposit (the class default is filled in), and the delivery and pickup fees: each is one way, an empty pickup fee is the delivery fee, and 0 means not offered.
4. Read What renters pay under the fields: real prices for a weekend, a few weekdays, a week and a month, worked out the way bookings are priced. Press **Save the rates**.

| Rate | What it means |
| --- | --- |
| Daily rate | A price per day, for each day that starts on a Sunday, Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday or Thursday |
| Weekend rate | A price per day, not for the whole weekend: each day that starts on a Friday or Saturday. Friday 10 am to Sunday 10 am is 2 days at this rate; Sunday to Monday is a daily day |
| Weekly rate | The price for 7 days. Rentals of 7 to 29 days cost this for each 7 days, counted by the day. A 1 to 6 day rental never costs more |
| Monthly rate | The price for 30 days. A 7 to 29 day rental never costs more |

5. Lead-time pricing for this car, below the rates: **Program settings** (the tiers there), **Off for this car**, or **Its own tiers** (a table like the one in Program settings). Press **Save**.
6. **Price limits**, beside them: the lowest and highest daily rate the owner accepts. **This car** sets the car''s own; the owner''s line sets them for every car of that owner (a car''s own come first, field by field). Empty is no limit. Press **Save price limits**. Owners set the same limits in their portal.

> Good to know: Price limits hold the rental a day (after lead-time pricing, the non-refundable discount, a discount, a promo code or a price typed by hand; never fees, add-ons or tax) between the minimum and the maximum: one line, "Minimum daily rate for this car" or "Maximum daily rate for this car", brings it back. Never on an Owner Booking or a booking billed to an insurer. To price one request outside them, open its review screen, **More options**, tick **Allow a price outside the car''s price limits (Admin only)** and say why: it is kept on the booking and in the audit log. Untick it and the limits apply again.

> Tip: A problem shows on its own field, in words, as you type. When similar cars have rates, a line suggests them with Use these; it is only a hint. The same fields are on **Add a car**, so a car can be added with its rates in one pass.

## Fleet tracking

**Cars** > **Vehicles**, the **Fleet tracking** tab. Fleet staff have the same map as **Fleet map** in their menu, and field staff see the cars of their own jobs under **Map**. Every car on the same map as the Live map, with who has it. Positions are seen by Admins and fleet staff only.

1. The four numbers: cars on rent, moving, parked, and open alerts.
2. The map shows each car as its photo in a ring: green moving (the arrow is its heading), yellow engine on, blue parked, orange not reporting. The list beside it has every car with its renter, booking, when it is due back (late in red) and its state.
3. Press a car on the map or in the list for its card: last report, odometer, fuel, tracker battery, whether the tracker has the car''s power, and the trip under way.
4. **Alerts**: speeding, left Ontario, left your zone, still driving after the return time, low tracker battery, unplugged and not reporting. Each also comes to the bell and, with phone alerts on, under Urgent alerts. Press **Show** to see where, **Seen** when it is handled, or **Mark all as seen**.
5. **Trips by booking**: each booking''s trips, kilometres and top speed (red at the speeding level). Press the last trip to draw its route on the map.

## Pair a tracker with a car

1. A new tracker that reports shows under **Trackers**, "Reporting, not on a car yet". Press **Pair**, choose the car and the install date.
2. Or press **Pair a tracker** and type its device ID (the IMEI or serial number on the tracker).
3. The install date starts the Tracker Fee on the owner''s invoice when the car has none yet. A replacement tracker keeps the car''s first date; the old tracker is taken off by itself.
4. **Remove** takes a tracker off a car (tick "faulty" for a broken one). The Tracker Fee is not changed.

## Tracking settings

Below the trackers: the speeding level (140 km/h), the minutes of grace after the return time (15), the low battery level (20%), the hours before "not reporting" (6), the Ontario alert, and one optional zone (a name, its centre and a radius in km). History keeps a moving car''s position once a minute for 90 days, trips and alerts for 365 days (at most 365: the privacy policy keeps tracker data 12 months).

1. Demo mode (off): simulated cars drive the GTA''s highways here and on the Live map, for a demonstration. Nothing is saved. Turn it off before the trackers go live.
2. **Make the ingest key**: the relay or tracker service signs every batch of positions with it. It is shown once; making a new one stops the old one at once.

> Tip: The Live map shows the same cars with its Fleet layer (tick Fleet).

## The listing pipeline

Open **Cars** > **Listings**. A draft waiting for review shows Needs review.

1. Each row shows the car, plate, state, photos and the work done on it so far.
2. Press **Start a listing** to begin one for a car that has none.
3. Open a car to review it.

![](/guides/img/admin-09-listings-desktop-970819b6.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 560; address: carmacars.ca/admin/listings; pins: 1 53.5 37.0, 2 87.2 21.1, 3 32.6 37.0")

## Review a listing

1. Steps to go live shows four numbered steps: **1 Photos** (how many of the required photos are in, 14 for most cars, 13 for a two-seater with no rear seats), **2 Cover plates**, **3 Review** and **4 Live on the site**. Each says what it needs and has one button to where it is done; the step to do now is in red. A step that stopped (a photo edit or the copy) shows under them with **Retry**.
2. Similar cars on file lists possible duplicates. Press **Not a duplicate** or **Same car**. An open flag does not keep the car off the site; only Same car does.
3. The copy is written by itself from the car''s facts and published when it passes the checks: nothing to type. To change a line, press Change; that field is then locked and kept by every new version.
4. Under Photos, each public photo shows its plate state: Plate not checked, Plate covered or No plate visible.

![](/guides/img/admin-10-listing-review-desktop-352745fd.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 1100; address: carmacars.ca/admin/listings/704abf3d-8905-443d-a157-d52769cf7449; pins: 1 20.6 16.6, 2 86.1 47.5, 3 19.9 106.8, 4 74.9 106.8")

## Cover the licence plate

On each public photo press **Cover the plate**. The editor opens.

1. The box over the plate is already suggested: as soon as the review opens, every outside photo (the More outside photos included) gets its suggestion, and those photos show Box suggested. Check it. **Suggest the plate** asks again.
2. Drag over a plate to draw a box. Drag a box to move it, or its corner to resize it.
3. Under Cover the plate with, keep **The CARMA Ontario plate** (on a rear plate: the company''s own Ontario plate CARMA, drawn in the photo''s perspective and light) or **Edit the front plate out** (on a front photo: the bumper is filled in, no box), or choose **A CarmaCars plate**, **Pixelation** or **Blur**. Photos covered the old way are made again the new way by themselves.
4. Press **Save the covered photo**. **Clear the boxes** starts over.
5. No plate in the shot? Press **No plate visible on this photo**.

![](/guides/img/admin-11-plate-editor-desktop-4219ad93.jpg "desktop; size: 690 703; address: carmacars.ca/admin/listings/704abf3d-8905-443d-a157-d52769cf7449; pins: 1 42.5 83.8, 2 49.6 29.9, 3 4.3 77.4, 4 15.5 83.8, 5 18.1 91.2")

> Tip: The covered photo replaces the public one; the original is kept privately. Keyboard: N adds a box, the arrows move it, Shift and the arrows resize it, Delete removes it.

## Publish

1. A real car that is not on the site is a line on To do: press **Set rates and publish**. The daily rate is filled in (the car''s own, or the suggested rate from similar cars or the class); change it if you like and press **Publish now**.
2. On the car itself, the Listing tab has **Publish now**; each open item of its checklist has a button to where it is done.
3. From a listing review: press **Approve and publish**, **Approve, publish later**, or **Send back** with what to fix.

> Watch out: The plate check never holds a car back: a real photo whose plate is not checked stays private (the other photos, or the sample photos, show instead) and goes public by itself once its plate is covered or marked not visible. Listings already live show "Plate not checked" on such photos.

## Photos filed under the wrong shot, and interior windows

1. On the Photos card, each shot lists its photos. A photo filed under the wrong shot: press **Remove** under it, then **Remove it**. The shot is free again: take or pick the right photo. The removed photo is kept privately and the removal is in the history. A live listing''s photos change in the review instead (Reject).
2. Dashboard and seat photos: what shows through the windows is replaced by the studio background when the cut is clean (a quality check: some but not most of the frame seen through, high in the frame, a few clean regions, sharp edges). Otherwise the windows are blurred, and the photo is marked windows blurred. Nothing to do.
3. A car with 2 seats or fewer needs no Rear seats photo.

## A listing without photos yet: sample photos

A car can be listed before its photos are taken. Until then the site shows a sample photo.

1. Submit the listing without photos. The listing copy is still written for you from the car''s details.
2. The car page and the car''s card show a sample photo, captioned "Sample photo", so renters know it is not this car. Staff see "Using sample photos" on the car and in Listings.
3. Publishing does not wait for a plate check: a sample photo has no plate.
4. Add the real photos when they are taken. Once real photos are approved they replace the sample at once; nothing else to do.

## Sample photos

**Settings** > **Sample photos**. The pictures a car shows until its real photos are in.

1. Every body type has a built-in picture (sedan, SUV, truck, van, coupe, hatchback, electric car).
2. Add your own: choose the Body type, and a Make and Model if the photo is of that exact model, pick the Photo, and press **Add the photo**.
3. The most specific photo wins: make and model, then make and body type, then body type. **Turn off** or **Delete** a photo you no longer want.
4. Cars using sample photos lists the cars still waiting for real photos. Each real car showing sample photos is also a line on To do, with **Add photos**.

![](/guides/img/admin-36-sample-photos-desktop-55c64070.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 812; address: carmacars.ca/admin/settings/sample-photos; pins: 4 26.8 28.9")

## Publish now, and new cars published by themselves

Nothing between a new car and the site has to be finished first: the car goes on the site, and what is still open shows on its checklist.

1. **Settings** > **Program**, **Publish new cars automatically** (on by default): a new real car goes on the site by itself as soon as it has its year, make and model and its rates, when it is added with rates, when its rates are saved, when it is added for an owner, or when an owner''s application is approved.
2. Otherwise open the car: its Listing tab says why it is not on the site and has **Publish now**. A car with no rates yet is published with the suggested rates (similar cars, else the class defaults in Program settings); change them later on the Rates tab.
3. Every real car has its listing from the moment it is added, as a draft. It shows in Listings and in Not on the site yet until it is published.
4. An owner''s own application waits for your decision before its car is published by itself; Publish now still works.
5. A car taken off the site by staff, or scheduled for a later date, is never published by itself: press **Publish now**.

## The checklist: what is still open on a listed car

Open items never stop publishing. They show as warnings on the car''s Listing tab and after Publish now.

| Item | What it means |
| --- | --- |
| Paperwork | Ownership permit, registry forms, agreements signed, Forms C and D, upfront payment, registry visit, tracker, safety certificate |
| Insurance | Not on the fleet insurance policy yet: the car can be booked, but not handed over |
| Details | Colour, body, seats, gearbox: the car page leaves out what is missing |
| Photos | No real photos: sample photos stand in. A photo whose plate is not checked stays private until it is |
| No VIN yet | A car added by its plate alone: add the VIN when you have it |
| Possible duplicate | An open flag in Similar cars. Only Same car keeps the car off the site |
| Owner terms | The management fee (Revenue Share) and fees not set: a request uses the owner''s terms or the standard grid |

## The fleet policy rule at handover

A program owner''s car is listed and can be requested, offered and paid for while its paperwork is open. It is never handed over until the insurer confirms in writing that it is on the fleet insurance policy.

- Staff see a warning on a request and an offer for a car not on the policy yet.
- The handover refuses the car until the insurer''s confirmation is recorded (Owners and onboarding). The field app says so on the job.
- Only real states keep a car off the site: retired, left the program, out of service, Turo only, bookings turned off, a self-managed owner in arrears, or a paused listing.

## Cars on sample photos

**Cars**, **Listings** ends with **Cars on sample photos**: each real car whose page still shows sample photos, with its newest handover photos (the check-in and check-out photos field staff take).

1. Where a handover photographed the car, press **Use the handover photos**. They go into the car''s listing as if taken on the capture screen.
2. When every required shot is there, the listing is submitted: the studio editor puts the car on the CarmaCars backdrop, then the listing waits for your review like any other.
3. A car with no handover photos yet gets them at its next handover, or press **Start a listing** and take them.

> Good to know: The studio editor uses Cloudflare image transformations (5,000 a month included). Settings > Usage counts them.

## A car''s registration and documents

Open the car, then **Owner & documents**. The **Registration** card:

1. Correct the **VIN** (it is checked: 17 characters, the check digit, not on another car; decoded again for the body style and trim), the **Year** and the **Body style**.
2. Type the **Ontario permit number** and the date the **Plate sticker expires**. Fleet gets a task 30 days and 7 days before; save the new date after the renewal and the task closes.
3. Under **Documents**, choose the kind (**Ownership permit**, Safety Standards Certificate, owner''s insurance, other), pick the photo or PDF and press **Upload**. The ownership permit clears that item of the owner''s checklist.
4. For the **Safety Standards Certificate**, also type its number, the date it was issued and the date it expires. Fleet gets a task 30 days and 7 days before it expires; upload the new certificate with its dates and the task closes. It is a document on the car, not a service record, and nothing is billed to the owner.
5. **Add a car** takes the ownership permit and the Safety Standards Certificate too, under **Documents (optional)**.

## A car added under the wrong owner

Open the car, Overview, **Who supplies the car**, **Move to another owner**. Choose the owner, or **CarmaCars (owner not known yet)**: the car becomes a company car, with no owner schedule or terms.

- The car''s unsigned owner application and vehicle schedule are withdrawn (kept in the history), and its draft owner invoices are deleted. Nobody is notified.
- It is refused once anything for the car is signed, issued, paid or on a statement.

### The VIN from the car, not typed

Every VIN field (Add a car, Add a car for an owner, the car''s **Registration**, **Start a listing**) has **Scan the barcode** and **Photo of the VIN**. Scan the barcode in the driver''s door frame or at the bottom of the windshield: the phone''s camera reads it by itself. Or take a photo of the VIN plate or sticker: the barcode in it is read first, else the photo is read for the printed VIN. The VIN is checked (17 characters, the check digit; I, O and Q become 1 and 0) and decoded as when you type it. Check it against the car before saving.

### Photos in any order

**Add photos** on the listing takes any number of photos at once from the camera roll. Each is sorted to its shot by itself (front three-quarter, sides, rear, dashboard, seats and the rest); a shot that already has its photo sends the new one to the extra photos, so nothing is replaced by accident. The shots are a guide, not a rule: a listing is complete with 10 photos that can go on the site and one outside photo for the cover. Outside photos get the studio background: the car is cropped to its edges and placed big in the frame with its wheels on the floor and a soft shadow under the tyres, and any corner watermark or caption beside the car is left out. Inside and detail photos are kept as taken; when one has a watermark, a logo or caption text on it, the edge with the mark is cut off by itself, and a photo whose mark cannot be cut off (one in the middle) stays off the site until you replace it. **Cover the plate** opens on every outside photo with the plate box suggested; check it and save.

Outside photos made before the newest framing (the car small in the frame, or without the model''s name behind it) are made again with **Frame the outside photos again** above the photos of the listing, then **Yes, frame again**. The cover and the main outside views get the model''s name lettered behind the car, as on the sample photos (for example CLA, C CLASS, AMG GT). The photos leave the site until their plates are checked again: the plate box is suggested on the new photos; check each and cover it. On a published listing each goes back on the site once its plate is checked.

## Showroom photos

Outside photos go in the CarmaCars showroom by themselves. When a real photographed room is stored (dealership or studio photos licensed for commercial use, fetched once from Wikimedia Commons with their author and licence kept), the car stands in it: about 70% of the width, its wheels on the room''s floor, a soft shadow and a faint reflection under it, its light matched to the room, and no sign or lettering on the real wall. Program settings > Listings has the switch (Photographed showroom rooms, on), the car''s width and the cut-out quality floor: a cut-out that is not clean enough (pieces, a blurry or ragged edge) is never placed in a room, the real photo is used instead (its plate covered as usual) and the photo says so. Without a stored room it is the drawn dark showroom: a simple dark dealership with linear lights in the ceiling, a slatted wood wall between two light strips with a big lit CarmaCars sign, and a polished dark floor with the car''s reflection and a shadow under each tyre. Every angle of a car is in the same room, and the cover has the model''s name in metal letters on the wall under the sign. The image model may relight the car or turn it slightly; a photo that shows another car, model or colour is not used. **Settings** > **Program settings** > **Listings** has the switch (Showroom photos, on), the image model that makes the photos look photographed, and its daily limit. Past the limit, or when the image model is not available, the site makes the showroom itself for free, and the photo says why under it.

- A car whose photos were made on the black studio: press **Apply showroom to this car** above its photos, then **Yes, apply**.
- Every car at once: **Listings** > **Showroom photos** > **Apply showroom to every car**, then **Yes, every car**.
- Under a photo in the showroom: **Redo** makes it again, **Back to the original** puts back the version before the showroom.

A car that stays where it was keeps its plate check. When the image model made the photo, check the plate again: the photo is off the site until you do. Photos made in the first showroom are made again in the new one with **Apply showroom to this car** or **Apply showroom to every car**.

## Failed photos

The site makes the photo sizes itself: the image service is asked only to cut the car out (**Settings** > **Program settings** > **Listings**: the switch to let the image service make every photo step is off). When the image service is busy or over its allowance, the photo still goes on the site from the original and is made again later. A listing marked Failed has **Retry failed photos** in its note; **Retry failed photos** at the top does every listing. They are made again a few at a time, and the listing leaves Failed when they are done.

## The first photo: plain, with a model, or a flyer

On a listing, under **First photo**, choose what shows first on the site and in the Marketplace kit. Switch any time; the other photos stay as they are.

- **Plain car**: the cover photo as it is (the default).
- **With a model**: a car-show photo made by the image model, with a fully clothed adult model beside the car. It needs the image model; until it is made (or when the image model is not there) the plain cover shows, and the listing says why.
- **Flyer**: the cover photo with a band like a printed flyer: the car, the price a day from its live rates, the call to action, a badge and the logo. When the price, the words or the cover photo change, it is made again by itself within 10 minutes; the plain cover shows meanwhile.

**Make it again** makes the chosen one again. The words of the flyer and the description of the model are in **Settings** > **Program settings** > **Listings** (First photo "flyer" and First photo "with a model"); {car}, {price}, {weekly} and {monthly} are filled for each car.

## Marketing photos in other scenes

For Marketplace and social posts, a car''s outside photos can be made again in other scenes. The website keeps its own photos in the dark showroom: a marketing set never replaces them.

1. On a listing, under **Marketing photos**, choose a scene, or **Mix: a different scene on each photo**, and press **Make the marketing set**.
2. The copies show as they are made. The dark showroom and the plain white studio are made by the site when the image model is not there; the photographic scenes (a bright showroom, a city street at night, the Toronto waterfront, a parking garage, Highway, a scenic road, Brick building) need the image model, and say so on the copy when it is not there.
3. **Download (ZIP)** takes the set; the Marketplace kit''s **With scenes (ZIP)** takes the same set.

**Settings** > **Program settings** > **Marketing scenes** lists the scenes. A scene made in a real place has a photo of that place: Brick building picks its photo by itself: the widest outside photo, as taken, of the shareholders'' own cars. To use another, press **Change the reference photo** and pick one (the shareholders'' cars'' photos come first), or upload one. The scenes'' names and words are in the **Marketing scenes** setting.

## Extra photos

A photo that fits no shot is an extra photo. Under the shots, **Extra outside photos** (put on the studio background) and **Extra inside and detail photos** (touched up) each take any number at once. They count toward the 10 photos, get the same plate check, and come after the standard shots on the car''s page.

1. In the review, **Extra photos, in their order on the car page** lists them.
2. Drag a photo by its handle (⋮⋮), or press **Earlier** or **Later**.
3. Press **Save the order**.

## Fix a cut-out

When the background removal cuts badly (a mirror or a wheel missing, background left beside the car), press **Edit the cut-out** under the outside photo.

1. **Cut-out** shows the car over the photo as taken, shown faintly. Choose **Erase** and brush over what should go, or **Restore** and brush over what the cut-out took off. Set **Brush size** and **Zoom**; when zoomed, **Move the view** pans. **Undo** takes back the last stroke.
2. **On the studio** shows the car on the studio background. Drag the car to move it and use **Size** to make it larger or smaller. **Centre and full size** puts it back.
3. Press **Save as a new version**. The photo is made again in about a minute; the version before and the photo as taken are kept. **Reset to the automatic cut-out** starts again from the automatic one.

> Good to know: If the car did not move, the plate check carries over: a photo marked no plate visible stays so, and a covered plate is covered again on the new photo when the review is open. If the car moved, check the plate again. A photo made before cut-outs were kept shows **Make the cut-out** first; the editor opens by itself when it is ready.

Every photo also gets a light touch-up by itself (exposure, levels, a little contrast and colour, mild sharpening), never enough to change the paint colour or hide a scratch. Turn it off for one photo with **Use original colours** under it (the photo is made again; approve it again), or for every photo in Admin > Settings > **Program settings** (Listings) with **Auto-enhance listing photos**. The photo as uploaded is always kept.
## Import photos from a Google Drive link

The owner often hands over a car''s photos as a public Google Drive folder, or one big folder with a folder per make and then per car. You do not download them: paste the link.

**One car.** On the car''s listing, under the capture, **Import photos from a Google Drive link**. Paste the folder link (shared with Anyone with the link) and press **Import the photos**. Every photo in the folder, and in the folders inside it, is added to this car as if you had pressed Add photos: each is sorted to its shot (else filed as an extra photo, in file-name order), put on the studio background and checked for its plate. The box under the link, **Submit the listing for processing when its photos are in**, is on by default.

**Many cars.** **Cars** > **Import photos from Drive** (a button on Vehicles). Paste the top folder''s link and press **Read the folder**. The page walks every folder and proposes a car for each folder that holds photos, from the year, make, model, colour and plate in the folder names (the make folder above counts; 01 Motors partner cars come first). Check the table: tick or untick **Import**, change the car in the list (the likely cars come first), leave out a folder with **Do not import this folder**. A line marked **Check this one** matched two alike cars. Then press **Import N photos from M folders**.

1. The page follows the import by itself. You can leave it and come back: it runs in the background.
2. The end shows the summary: imported, skipped and failed, and why for each (a file over 15 MB, a file that is not a photo, the same photo already on the car, a folder not shared).
3. **Try the failed photos again** takes only the ones that failed. Pressing Import on the same link again never adds a photo twice: a Drive file already on the car is skipped, and so is the same picture under another name. A photo you took off the car can be imported again.

> Good to know: JPG, PNG, HEIC and WebP only (HEIC and WebP are made JPEG first). At most 15 MB a photo, 600 photos, 400 folders and 4 GB in one import. Drive is asked politely, one photo at a time; a big import takes a while.

> Good to know: Without a key, Drive shows only the first 50 files of a folder on its public page; a folder with more is read in full when Drive allows it. In **Settings**, the **Photo import from Google Drive** box takes a Google API key with the Drive API on (after it is saved only its last 4 characters are shown, and it is never written to the change log): with it, folders of any size are read and photos download without Drive''s warning pages.

## Test bookings and deleting a car

1. On a booking made only to try the site, press **Mark as a test booking** (Admins only; the reason is optional). **Make it a real booking again** undoes it.
2. A car whose bookings are all test bookings can be deleted: the test bookings and their test payments go with it, and a copy is kept in the archive of deleted requests.
3. A car with a real booking cannot be deleted.

## Pickup from owner and return to owner (release 28)

On a car''s page, **Pickup from owner and return to owner** records the car''s condition when CarmaCars picks it up from its owner or gives it back: the date and time, km, fuel, many photos at once with the suggested angles, and notes. **Add photos** adds more to a record later. The owner sees these records read only on the car''s page in their portal. They are the baseline condition for any dispute.

## Incident cards (release 34)
**Cars** > **Vehicles** > **Incident cards** prints the card for each car: what to do in an accident or a breakdown, the support number from Settings, a roadside number when there is one, a QR code to report it in the app, and the fleet insurance slip. Open a car and press **Incident card** to print only that car; on the list, **Print all cars** prints them all, two cards to a Letter page with crop marks, ready to laminate. Under Fleet insurance policy press **Add the policy** (the insurer, the policy number, the dates, the named insured, the roadside number on the slip) and choose the uploaded slip if you have one: it is printed as it is, otherwise the fields are. The card never shows a premium. Fleet staff print the same cards from their portal.

## Field jobs, shifts and who gets a job

**Cars**, then **Field jobs**, is the board Fleet uses, with every action Fleet has. Field staff take shifts you publish with **Publish shifts**. Jobs go on shifts, not on people: each job is put on the shift covering its time (or that day''s), whoever holds the shift does it (several people share the jobs, least busy first), a shift nobody holds keeps its jobs for whoever claims it, and work lands only on days with shifts (work due on a day without shifts moves to the day before, or to the next day with shifts when it comes in on the day; the booking''s own times never change). A booking whose handover or return falls on a day with no shifts shows a warning on the board and on the booking. **To a shift** moves a job to another shift. You can give a job to a field person on a shift that day or to an Admin, take it off with **Unassign** (tick **Tell them** to let them know), and an Admin who holds a job opens it on the field portal. A person who has not passed the academy cannot be given a job or take a shift. A shift with jobs and nobody on it within 24 hours alerts Fleet and the Admins once.', 'Fleet and listings', 'Vehicles, the listing pipeline, similar cars and covering licence plates.',
  'Vehicles is the fleet. Listings turns a car into a page on carmacars.ca in four steps: photos, covered plates, a review, and live on the site.

## Vehicles

**Cars** > **Vehicles**

1. Filter by status; More filters has who supplies the car, retired cars and the mode. Each row shows the plate, class, owner, mode, status, listing and daily rate.
2. Search by plate, model or owner. **Cars** > **Rates for many cars** changes the rates of many cars at once.
3. Open a car for its tabs: Overview, Rates, Fees and coverage, Calendar, Listing, and Owner, documents, tracker. The Tracker card links to Fleet tracking.

![](/guides/img/admin-08-vehicles-desktop-46461f49.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 900; address: carmacars.ca/admin/vehicles; pins: 1 74.3 31.1, 2 37.5 24.3, 3 48.6 52.4")

## Set a car''s rates and kilometres

Open the car, then the **Rates** tab. Everything on it saves together, in one step.

1. Type the four rates. Only the daily rate is needed: an empty weekend rate is the daily rate, an empty weekly rate is 6 days at the daily rate, and an empty monthly rate is 22 days.
2. Kilometres: keep **Use the defaults** (the kilometres a day in Settings, Kilometre choices, and the extra kilometre rate in Fee defaults for the car''s class), or choose **Custom for this car** and type them.
3. Check the deposit (the class default is filled in), and the delivery and pickup fees: each is one way, an empty pickup fee is the delivery fee, and 0 means not offered.
4. Read What renters pay under the fields: real prices for a weekend, a few weekdays, a week and a month, worked out the way bookings are priced. Press **Save the rates**.

| Rate | What it means |
| --- | --- |
| Daily rate | A price per day, for each day that starts on a Sunday, Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday or Thursday |
| Weekend rate | A price per day, not for the whole weekend: each day that starts on a Friday or Saturday. Friday 10 am to Sunday 10 am is 2 days at this rate; Sunday to Monday is a daily day |
| Weekly rate | The price for 7 days. Rentals of 7 to 29 days cost this for each 7 days, counted by the day. A 1 to 6 day rental never costs more |
| Monthly rate | The price for 30 days. A 7 to 29 day rental never costs more |

5. Lead-time pricing for this car, below the rates: **Program settings** (the tiers there), **Off for this car**, or **Its own tiers** (a table like the one in Program settings). Press **Save**.
6. **Price limits**, beside them: the lowest and highest daily rate the owner accepts. **This car** sets the car''s own; the owner''s line sets them for every car of that owner (a car''s own come first, field by field). Empty is no limit. Press **Save price limits**. Owners set the same limits in their portal.

> Good to know: Price limits hold the rental a day (after lead-time pricing, the non-refundable discount, a discount, a promo code or a price typed by hand; never fees, add-ons or tax) between the minimum and the maximum: one line, "Minimum daily rate for this car" or "Maximum daily rate for this car", brings it back. Never on an Owner Booking or a booking billed to an insurer. To price one request outside them, open its review screen, **More options**, tick **Allow a price outside the car''s price limits (Admin only)** and say why: it is kept on the booking and in the audit log. Untick it and the limits apply again.

> Tip: A problem shows on its own field, in words, as you type. When similar cars have rates, a line suggests them with Use these; it is only a hint. The same fields are on **Add a car**, so a car can be added with its rates in one pass.

## Fleet tracking

**Cars** > **Vehicles**, the **Fleet tracking** tab. Fleet staff have the same map as **Fleet map** in their menu, and field staff see the cars of their own jobs under **Map**. Every car on the same map as the Live map, with who has it. Positions are seen by Admins and fleet staff only.

1. The four numbers: cars on rent, moving, parked, and open alerts.
2. The map shows each car as its photo in a ring: green moving (the arrow is its heading), yellow engine on, blue parked, orange not reporting. The list beside it has every car with its renter, booking, when it is due back (late in red) and its state.
3. Press a car on the map or in the list for its card: last report, odometer, fuel, tracker battery, whether the tracker has the car''s power, and the trip under way.
4. **Alerts**: speeding, left Ontario, left your zone, still driving after the return time, low tracker battery, unplugged and not reporting. Each also comes to the bell and, with phone alerts on, under Urgent alerts. Press **Show** to see where, **Seen** when it is handled, or **Mark all as seen**.
5. **Trips by booking**: each booking''s trips, kilometres and top speed (red at the speeding level). Press the last trip to draw its route on the map.

## Pair a tracker with a car

1. A new tracker that reports shows under **Trackers**, "Reporting, not on a car yet". Press **Pair**, choose the car and the install date.
2. Or press **Pair a tracker** and type its device ID (the IMEI or serial number on the tracker).
3. The install date starts the Tracker Fee on the owner''s invoice when the car has none yet. A replacement tracker keeps the car''s first date; the old tracker is taken off by itself.
4. **Remove** takes a tracker off a car (tick "faulty" for a broken one). The Tracker Fee is not changed.

## Tracking settings

Below the trackers: the speeding level (140 km/h), the minutes of grace after the return time (15), the low battery level (20%), the hours before "not reporting" (6), the Ontario alert, and one optional zone (a name, its centre and a radius in km). History keeps a moving car''s position once a minute for 90 days, trips and alerts for 365 days (at most 365: the privacy policy keeps tracker data 12 months).

1. Demo mode (off): simulated cars drive the GTA''s highways here and on the Live map, for a demonstration. Nothing is saved. Turn it off before the trackers go live.
2. **Make the ingest key**: the relay or tracker service signs every batch of positions with it. It is shown once; making a new one stops the old one at once.

> Tip: The Live map shows the same cars with its Fleet layer (tick Fleet).

## The listing pipeline

Open **Cars** > **Listings**. A draft waiting for review shows Needs review.

1. Each row shows the car, plate, state, photos and the work done on it so far.
2. Press **Start a listing** to begin one for a car that has none.
3. Open a car to review it.

![](/guides/img/admin-09-listings-desktop-970819b6.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 560; address: carmacars.ca/admin/listings; pins: 1 53.5 37.0, 2 87.2 21.1, 3 32.6 37.0")

## Review a listing

1. Steps to go live shows four numbered steps: **1 Photos** (how many of the required photos are in, 14 for most cars, 13 for a two-seater with no rear seats), **2 Cover plates**, **3 Review** and **4 Live on the site**. Each says what it needs and has one button to where it is done; the step to do now is in red. A step that stopped (a photo edit or the copy) shows under them with **Retry**.
2. Similar cars on file lists possible duplicates. Press **Not a duplicate** or **Same car**. An open flag does not keep the car off the site; only Same car does.
3. The copy is written by itself from the car''s facts and published when it passes the checks: nothing to type. To change a line, press Change; that field is then locked and kept by every new version.
4. Under Photos, each public photo shows its plate state: Plate not checked, Plate covered or No plate visible.

![](/guides/img/admin-10-listing-review-desktop-352745fd.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 1100; address: carmacars.ca/admin/listings/704abf3d-8905-443d-a157-d52769cf7449; pins: 1 20.6 16.6, 2 86.1 47.5, 3 19.9 106.8, 4 74.9 106.8")

## Cover the licence plate

The plates are checked by themselves. Every photo is looked at by the vision model within the day''s free AI share: a plate it finds is covered (the photo shows Covered automatically, with how sure it was), a photo with no plate is marked No plate visible (No plate seen automatically), and a photo it is not sure of stays Plate not checked for you. While photos wait, the Photos card says how many. A wrong decision: press **Undo** on the photo (the photo as it was comes back, Plate not checked), or **Not a plate: no plate visible** on a cover put where there is no plate.

To cover a plate yourself, press **Cover the plate** on the photo. The editor opens right under it.

1. Check the box over the plate, or press **Suggest the plate**.
2. Drag over a plate to draw a box. Drag a box to move it, or its corner to resize it.
3. Under Cover the plate with, keep **The CARMA Ontario plate** (on a rear plate: the company''s own Ontario plate CARMA, drawn in the photo''s perspective and light) or **Edit the front plate out** (on a front photo: the bumper is filled in, no box), or choose **A CarmaCars plate**, **Pixelation** or **Blur**. Photos covered the old way are made again the new way by themselves.
4. Press **Save the covered photo**. **Clear the boxes** starts over.
5. No plate in the shot? Press **No plate visible on this photo**.

![](/guides/img/admin-11-plate-editor-desktop-4219ad93.jpg "desktop; size: 690 703; address: carmacars.ca/admin/listings/704abf3d-8905-443d-a157-d52769cf7449; pins: 1 42.5 83.8, 2 49.6 29.9, 3 4.3 77.4, 4 15.5 83.8, 5 18.1 91.2")

> Tip: The covered photo replaces the public one; the original is kept privately. Keyboard: N adds a box, the arrows move it, Shift and the arrows resize it, Delete removes it.

## Publish

1. A real car that is not on the site is a line on To do: press **Set rates and publish**. The daily rate is filled in (the car''s own, or the suggested rate from similar cars or the class); change it if you like and press **Publish now**.
2. On the car itself, the Listing tab has **Publish now**; each open item of its checklist has a button to where it is done.
3. From a listing review: press **Approve and publish**, **Approve, publish later**, or **Send back** with what to fix.

> Watch out: The plate check never holds a car back: a real photo whose plate is not checked stays private (the other photos, or the sample photos, show instead) and goes public by itself once its plate is covered or marked not visible. Listings already live show "Plate not checked" on such photos.

## Photos filed under the wrong shot, and interior windows

1. On the Photos card, each shot lists its photos. A photo filed under the wrong shot: press **Remove** under it, then **Remove it**. The shot is free again: take or pick the right photo. The removed photo is kept privately and the removal is in the history. A live listing''s photos change in the review instead (Reject).
2. Dashboard and seat photos: what shows through the windows is replaced by the studio background when the cut is clean (a quality check: some but not most of the frame seen through, high in the frame, a few clean regions, sharp edges). Otherwise the windows are blurred, and the photo is marked windows blurred. Nothing to do.
3. A car with 2 seats or fewer needs no Rear seats photo.

## A listing without photos yet: sample photos

A car can be listed before its photos are taken. Until then the site shows a sample photo.

1. Submit the listing without photos. The listing copy is still written for you from the car''s details.
2. The car page and the car''s card show a sample photo, captioned "Sample photo", so renters know it is not this car. Staff see "Using sample photos" on the car and in Listings.
3. Publishing does not wait for a plate check: a sample photo has no plate.
4. Add the real photos when they are taken. Once real photos are approved they replace the sample at once; nothing else to do.

## Sample photos

**Settings** > **Sample photos**. The pictures a car shows until its real photos are in.

1. Every body type has a built-in picture (sedan, SUV, truck, van, coupe, hatchback, electric car).
2. Add your own: choose the Body type, and a Make and Model if the photo is of that exact model, pick the Photo, and press **Add the photo**.
3. The most specific photo wins: make and model, then make and body type, then body type. **Turn off** or **Delete** a photo you no longer want.
4. Cars using sample photos lists the cars still waiting for real photos. Each real car showing sample photos is also a line on To do, with **Add photos**.

![](/guides/img/admin-36-sample-photos-desktop-55c64070.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 812; address: carmacars.ca/admin/settings/sample-photos; pins: 4 26.8 28.9")

## Publish now, and new cars published by themselves

Nothing between a new car and the site has to be finished first: the car goes on the site, and what is still open shows on its checklist.

1. **Settings** > **Program**, **Publish new cars automatically** (on by default): a new real car goes on the site by itself as soon as it has its year, make and model and its rates, when it is added with rates, when its rates are saved, when it is added for an owner, or when an owner''s application is approved.
2. Otherwise open the car: its Listing tab says why it is not on the site and has **Publish now**. A car with no rates yet is published with the suggested rates (similar cars, else the class defaults in Program settings); change them later on the Rates tab.
3. Every real car has its listing from the moment it is added, as a draft. It shows in Listings and in Not on the site yet until it is published.
4. An owner''s own application waits for your decision before its car is published by itself; Publish now still works.
5. A car taken off the site by staff, or scheduled for a later date, is never published by itself: press **Publish now**.

## The checklist: what is still open on a listed car

Open items never stop publishing. They show as warnings on the car''s Listing tab and after Publish now.

| Item | What it means |
| --- | --- |
| Paperwork | Ownership permit, registry forms, agreements signed, Forms C and D, upfront payment, registry visit, tracker, safety certificate |
| Insurance | Not on the fleet insurance policy yet: the car can be booked, but not handed over |
| Details | Colour, body, seats, gearbox: the car page leaves out what is missing |
| Photos | No real photos: sample photos stand in. A photo whose plate is not checked stays private until it is |
| No VIN yet | A car added by its plate alone: add the VIN when you have it |
| Possible duplicate | An open flag in Similar cars. Only Same car keeps the car off the site |
| Owner terms | The management fee (Revenue Share) and fees not set: a request uses the owner''s terms or the standard grid |

## The fleet policy rule at handover

A program owner''s car is listed and can be requested, offered and paid for while its paperwork is open. It is never handed over until the insurer confirms in writing that it is on the fleet insurance policy.

- Staff see a warning on a request and an offer for a car not on the policy yet.
- The handover refuses the car until the insurer''s confirmation is recorded (Owners and onboarding). The field app says so on the job.
- Only real states keep a car off the site: retired, left the program, out of service, Turo only, bookings turned off, a self-managed owner in arrears, or a paused listing.

## Cars on sample photos

**Cars**, **Listings** ends with **Cars on sample photos**: each real car whose page still shows sample photos, with its newest handover photos (the check-in and check-out photos field staff take).

1. Where a handover photographed the car, press **Use the handover photos**. They go into the car''s listing as if taken on the capture screen.
2. When every required shot is there, the listing is submitted: the studio editor puts the car on the CarmaCars backdrop, then the listing waits for your review like any other.
3. A car with no handover photos yet gets them at its next handover, or press **Start a listing** and take them.

> Good to know: The studio editor uses Cloudflare image transformations (5,000 a month included). Settings > Usage counts them.

## A car''s registration and documents

Open the car, then **Owner & documents**. The **Registration** card:

1. Correct the **VIN** (it is checked: 17 characters, the check digit, not on another car; decoded again for the body style and trim), the **Year** and the **Body style**.
2. Type the **Ontario permit number** and the date the **Plate sticker expires**. Fleet gets a task 30 days and 7 days before; save the new date after the renewal and the task closes.
3. Under **Documents**, choose the kind (**Ownership permit**, Safety Standards Certificate, owner''s insurance, other), pick the photo or PDF and press **Upload**. The ownership permit clears that item of the owner''s checklist.
4. For the **Safety Standards Certificate**, also type its number, the date it was issued and the date it expires. Fleet gets a task 30 days and 7 days before it expires; upload the new certificate with its dates and the task closes. It is a document on the car, not a service record, and nothing is billed to the owner.
5. **Add a car** takes the ownership permit and the Safety Standards Certificate too, under **Documents (optional)**.

## A car added under the wrong owner

Open the car, Overview, **Who supplies the car**, **Move to another owner**. Choose the owner, or **CarmaCars (owner not known yet)**: the car becomes a company car, with no owner schedule or terms.

- The car''s unsigned owner application and vehicle schedule are withdrawn (kept in the history), and its draft owner invoices are deleted. Nobody is notified.
- It is refused once anything for the car is signed, issued, paid or on a statement.

### The VIN from the car, not typed

Every VIN field (Add a car, Add a car for an owner, the car''s **Registration**, **Start a listing**) has **Scan the barcode** and **Photo of the VIN**. Scan the barcode in the driver''s door frame or at the bottom of the windshield: the phone''s camera reads it by itself. Or take a photo of the VIN plate or sticker: the barcode in it is read first, else the photo is read for the printed VIN. The VIN is checked (17 characters, the check digit; I, O and Q become 1 and 0) and decoded as when you type it. Check it against the car before saving.

### Photos in any order

**Add photos** on the listing takes any number of photos at once from the camera roll. Each is sorted to its shot by itself (front three-quarter, sides, rear, dashboard, seats and the rest); a shot that already has its photo sends the new one to the extra photos, so nothing is replaced by accident. The shots are a guide, not a rule: a listing is complete with 10 photos that can go on the site and one outside photo for the cover. Outside photos get the studio background: the car is cropped to its edges and placed big in the frame with its wheels on the floor and a soft shadow under the tyres, and any corner watermark or caption beside the car is left out. Inside and detail photos are kept as taken; when one has a watermark, a logo or caption text on it, the edge with the mark is cut off by itself, and a photo whose mark cannot be cut off (one in the middle) stays off the site until you replace it. **Cover the plate** opens on every outside photo with the plate box suggested; check it and save.

Outside photos made before the newest framing (the car small in the frame, or without the model''s name behind it) are made again with **Frame the outside photos again** above the photos of the listing, then **Yes, frame again**. The cover and the main outside views get the model''s name lettered behind the car, as on the sample photos (for example CLA, C CLASS, AMG GT). The photos leave the site until their plates are checked again: the plate box is suggested on the new photos; check each and cover it. On a published listing each goes back on the site once its plate is checked.

## Showroom photos

Outside photos go in the CarmaCars showroom by themselves. When a real photographed room is stored (dealership or studio photos licensed for commercial use, fetched once from Wikimedia Commons with their author and licence kept), the car stands in it: about 70% of the width, its wheels on the room''s floor, a soft shadow and a faint reflection under it, its light matched to the room, and no sign or lettering on the real wall. Program settings > Listings has the switch (Photographed showroom rooms, on), the car''s width and the cut-out quality floor: a cut-out that is not clean enough (pieces, a blurry or ragged edge) is never placed in a room, the real photo is used instead (its plate covered as usual) and the photo says so. Without a stored room it is the drawn dark showroom: a simple dark dealership with linear lights in the ceiling, a slatted wood wall between two light strips with a big lit CarmaCars sign, and a polished dark floor with the car''s reflection and a shadow under each tyre. Every angle of a car is in the same room, and the cover has the model''s name in metal letters on the wall under the sign. The image model may relight the car or turn it slightly; a photo that shows another car, model or colour is not used. **Settings** > **Program settings** > **Listings** has the switch (Showroom photos, on), the image model that makes the photos look photographed, and its daily limit. Past the limit, or when the image model is not available, the site makes the showroom itself for free, and the photo says why under it.

- A car whose photos were made on the black studio: press **Apply showroom to this car** above its photos, then **Yes, apply**.
- Every car at once: **Listings** > **Showroom photos** > **Apply showroom to every car**, then **Yes, every car**.
- Under a photo in the showroom: **Redo** makes it again, **Back to the original** puts back the version before the showroom.

A car that stays where it was keeps its plate check. When the image model made the photo, check the plate again: the photo is off the site until you do. Photos made in the first showroom are made again in the new one with **Apply showroom to this car** or **Apply showroom to every car**.

## Failed photos

The site makes the photo sizes itself: the image service is asked only to cut the car out (**Settings** > **Program settings** > **Listings**: the switch to let the image service make every photo step is off). When the image service is busy or over its allowance, the photo still goes on the site from the original and is made again later. A listing marked Failed has **Retry failed photos** in its note; **Retry failed photos** at the top does every listing. They are made again a few at a time, and the listing leaves Failed when they are done.

## The first photo: plain, with a model, or a flyer

On a listing, under **First photo**, choose what shows first on the site and in the Marketplace kit. Switch any time; the other photos stay as they are.

- **Plain car**: the cover photo as it is (the default).
- **With a model**: a car-show photo made by the image model, with a fully clothed adult model beside the car. It needs the image model; until it is made (or when the image model is not there) the plain cover shows, and the listing says why.
- **Flyer**: the cover photo with a band like a printed flyer: the car, the price a day from its live rates, the call to action, a badge and the logo. When the price, the words or the cover photo change, it is made again by itself within 10 minutes; the plain cover shows meanwhile.

**Make it again** makes the chosen one again. The words of the flyer and the description of the model are in **Settings** > **Program settings** > **Listings** (First photo "flyer" and First photo "with a model"); {car}, {price}, {weekly} and {monthly} are filled for each car.

## Marketing photos in other scenes

For Marketplace and social posts, a car''s outside photos can be made again in other scenes. The website keeps its own photos in the dark showroom: a marketing set never replaces them.

1. On a listing, under **Marketing photos**, choose a scene, or **Mix: a different scene on each photo**, and press **Make the marketing set**.
2. The copies show as they are made. The dark showroom and the plain white studio are made by the site when the image model is not there; the photographic scenes (a bright showroom, a city street at night, the Toronto waterfront, a parking garage, Highway, a scenic road, Brick building) need the image model, and say so on the copy when it is not there.
3. **Download (ZIP)** takes the set; the Marketplace kit''s **With scenes (ZIP)** takes the same set.

**Settings** > **Program settings** > **Marketing scenes** lists the scenes. A scene made in a real place has a photo of that place: Brick building picks its photo by itself: the widest outside photo, as taken, of the shareholders'' own cars. To use another, press **Change the reference photo** and pick one (the shareholders'' cars'' photos come first), or upload one. The scenes'' names and words are in the **Marketing scenes** setting.

## Extra photos

A photo that fits no shot is an extra photo. Under the shots, **Extra outside photos** (put on the studio background) and **Extra inside and detail photos** (touched up) each take any number at once. They count toward the 10 photos, get the same plate check, and come after the standard shots on the car''s page.

1. In the review, **Extra photos, in their order on the car page** lists them.
2. Drag a photo by its handle (⋮⋮), or press **Earlier** or **Later**.
3. Press **Save the order**.

## Fix a cut-out

When the background removal cuts badly (a mirror or a wheel missing, background left beside the car), press **Edit the cut-out** under the outside photo.

1. **Cut-out** shows the car over the photo as taken, shown faintly. Choose **Erase** and brush over what should go, or **Restore** and brush over what the cut-out took off. Set **Brush size** and **Zoom**; when zoomed, **Move the view** pans. **Undo** takes back the last stroke.
2. **On the studio** shows the car on the studio background. Drag the car to move it and use **Size** to make it larger or smaller. **Centre and full size** puts it back.
3. Press **Save as a new version**. The photo is made again in about a minute; the version before and the photo as taken are kept. **Reset to the automatic cut-out** starts again from the automatic one.

> Good to know: If the car did not move, the plate check carries over: a photo marked no plate visible stays so, and a covered plate is covered again on the new photo when the review is open. If the car moved, check the plate again. A photo made before cut-outs were kept shows **Make the cut-out** first; the editor opens by itself when it is ready.

Every photo also gets a light touch-up by itself (exposure, levels, a little contrast and colour, mild sharpening), never enough to change the paint colour or hide a scratch. Turn it off for one photo with **Use original colours** under it (the photo is made again; approve it again), or for every photo in Admin > Settings > **Program settings** (Listings) with **Auto-enhance listing photos**. The photo as uploaded is always kept.
## Import photos from a Google Drive link

The owner often hands over a car''s photos as a public Google Drive folder, or one big folder with a folder per make and then per car. You do not download them: paste the link.

**One car.** On the car''s listing, under the capture, **Import photos from a Google Drive link**. Paste the folder link (shared with Anyone with the link) and press **Import the photos**. Every photo in the folder, and in the folders inside it, is added to this car as if you had pressed Add photos: each is sorted to its shot (else filed as an extra photo, in file-name order), put on the studio background and checked for its plate. The box under the link, **Submit the listing for processing when its photos are in**, is on by default.

**Many cars.** **Cars** > **Import photos from Drive** (a button on Vehicles). Paste the top folder''s link and press **Read the folder**. The page walks every folder and proposes a car for each folder that holds photos, from the year, make, model, colour and plate in the folder names (the make folder above counts; 01 Motors partner cars come first). Check the table: tick or untick **Import**, change the car in the list (the likely cars come first), leave out a folder with **Do not import this folder**. A line marked **Check this one** matched two alike cars. Then press **Import N photos from M folders**.

1. The page follows the import by itself. You can leave it and come back: it runs in the background.
2. The end shows the summary: imported, skipped and failed, and why for each (a file over 15 MB, a file that is not a photo, the same photo already on the car, a folder not shared).
3. **Try the failed photos again** takes only the ones that failed. Pressing Import on the same link again never adds a photo twice: a Drive file already on the car is skipped, and so is the same picture under another name. A photo you took off the car can be imported again.

> Good to know: JPG, PNG, HEIC and WebP only (HEIC and WebP are made JPEG first). At most 15 MB a photo, 600 photos, 400 folders and 4 GB in one import. Drive is asked politely, one photo at a time; a big import takes a while.

> Good to know: Without a key, Drive shows only the first 50 files of a folder on its public page; a folder with more is read in full when Drive allows it. In **Settings**, the **Photo import from Google Drive** box takes a Google API key with the Drive API on (after it is saved only its last 4 characters are shown, and it is never written to the change log): with it, folders of any size are read and photos download without Drive''s warning pages.

## Test bookings and deleting a car

1. On a booking made only to try the site, press **Mark as a test booking** (Admins only; the reason is optional). **Make it a real booking again** undoes it.
2. A car whose bookings are all test bookings can be deleted: the test bookings and their test payments go with it, and a copy is kept in the archive of deleted requests.
3. A car with a real booking cannot be deleted.

## Pickup from owner and return to owner (release 28)

On a car''s page, **Pickup from owner and return to owner** records the car''s condition when CarmaCars picks it up from its owner or gives it back: the date and time, km, fuel, many photos at once with the suggested angles, and notes. **Add photos** adds more to a record later. The owner sees these records read only on the car''s page in their portal. They are the baseline condition for any dispute.

## Incident cards (release 34)
**Cars** > **Vehicles** > **Incident cards** prints the card for each car: what to do in an accident or a breakdown, the support number from Settings, a roadside number when there is one, a QR code to report it in the app, and the fleet insurance slip. Open a car and press **Incident card** to print only that car; on the list, **Print all cars** prints them all, two cards to a Letter page with crop marks, ready to laminate. Under Fleet insurance policy press **Add the policy** (the insurer, the policy number, the dates, the named insured, the roadside number on the slip) and choose the uploaded slip if you have one: it is printed as it is, otherwise the fields are. The card never shows a premium. Fleet staff print the same cards from their portal.

## Field jobs, shifts and who gets a job

**Cars**, then **Field jobs**, is the board Fleet uses, with every action Fleet has. Field staff take shifts you publish with **Publish shifts**. Jobs go on shifts, not on people: each job is put on the shift covering its time (or that day''s), whoever holds the shift does it (several people share the jobs, least busy first), a shift nobody holds keeps its jobs for whoever claims it, and work lands only on days with shifts (work due on a day without shifts moves to the day before, or to the next day with shifts when it comes in on the day; the booking''s own times never change). A booking whose handover or return falls on a day with no shifts shows a warning on the board and on the booking. **To a shift** moves a job to another shift. You can give a job to a field person on a shift that day or to an Admin, take it off with **Unassign** (tick **Tell them** to let them know), and an Admin who holds a job opens it on the field portal. A person who has not passed the academy cannot be given a job or take a shift. A shift with jobs and nobody on it within 24 hours alerts Fleet and the Admins once.',
  '<p class="gd-p">Vehicles is the fleet. Listings turns a car into a page on carmacars.ca in four steps: photos, covered plates, a review, and live on the site.</p><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-vehicles" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Vehicles</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Vehicles</b></p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Filter by status; More filters has who supplies the car, retired cars and the mode. Each row shows the plate, class, owner, mode, status, listing and daily rate.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Search by plate, model or owner. <b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Rates for many cars</b> changes the rates of many cars at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Open a car for its tabs: Overview, Rates, Fees and coverage, Calendar, Listing, and Owner, documents, tracker. The Tracker card links to Fleet tracking.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/vehicles</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/900"><img src="/guides/img/admin-08-vehicles-desktop-46461f49.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="900"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:74.3%;top:31.1%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:37.5%;top:24.3%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:48.6%;top:52.4%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-set-a-car-s-rates-and-kilometres" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Set a car&#39;s rates and kilometres</h2><p class="gd-p">Open the car, then the <b class="gd-ui">Rates</b> tab. Everything on it saves together, in one step.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Type the four rates. Only the daily rate is needed: an empty weekend rate is the daily rate, an empty weekly rate is 6 days at the daily rate, and an empty monthly rate is 22 days.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Kilometres: keep <b class="gd-ui">Use the defaults</b> (the kilometres a day in Settings, Kilometre choices, and the extra kilometre rate in Fee defaults for the car&#39;s class), or choose <b class="gd-ui">Custom for this car</b> and type them.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Check the deposit (the class default is filled in), and the delivery and pickup fees: each is one way, an empty pickup fee is the delivery fee, and 0 means not offered.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Read What renters pay under the fields: real prices for a weekend, a few weekdays, a week and a month, worked out the way bookings are priced. Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the rates</b>.</div></li></ol></div><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Rate</th><th scope="col">What it means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Daily rate</td><td>A price per day, for each day that starts on a Sunday, Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday or Thursday</td></tr><tr><td>Weekend rate</td><td>A price per day, not for the whole weekend: each day that starts on a Friday or Saturday. Friday 10 am to Sunday 10 am is 2 days at this rate; Sunday to Monday is a daily day</td></tr><tr><td>Weekly rate</td><td>The price for 7 days. Rentals of 7 to 29 days cost this for each 7 days, counted by the day. A 1 to 6 day rental never costs more</td></tr><tr><td>Monthly rate</td><td>The price for 30 days. A 7 to 29 day rental never costs more</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol" start="5"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Lead-time pricing for this car, below the rates: <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> (the tiers there), <b class="gd-ui">Off for this car</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Its own tiers</b> (a table like the one in Program settings). Press <b class="gd-ui">Save</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Price limits</b>, beside them: the lowest and highest daily rate the owner accepts. <b class="gd-ui">This car</b> sets the car&#39;s own; the owner&#39;s line sets them for every car of that owner (a car&#39;s own come first, field by field). Empty is no limit. Press <b class="gd-ui">Save price limits</b>. Owners set the same limits in their portal.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Price limits hold the rental a day (after lead-time pricing, the non-refundable discount, a discount, a promo code or a price typed by hand; never fees, add-ons or tax) between the minimum and the maximum: one line, &quot;Minimum daily rate for this car&quot; or &quot;Maximum daily rate for this car&quot;, brings it back. Never on an Owner Booking or a booking billed to an insurer. To price one request outside them, open its review screen, <b class="gd-ui">More options</b>, tick <b class="gd-ui">Allow a price outside the car&#39;s price limits (Admin only)</b> and say why: it is kept on the booking and in the audit log. Untick it and the limits apply again.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>A problem shows on its own field, in words, as you type. When similar cars have rates, a line suggests them with Use these; it is only a hint. The same fields are on <b class="gd-ui">Add a car</b>, so a car can be added with its rates in one pass.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-fleet-tracking" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Fleet tracking</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Vehicles</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Fleet tracking</b> tab. Fleet staff have the same map as <b class="gd-ui">Fleet map</b> in their menu, and field staff see the cars of their own jobs under <b class="gd-ui">Map</b>. Every car on the same map as the Live map, with who has it. Positions are seen by Admins and fleet staff only.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The four numbers: cars on rent, moving, parked, and open alerts.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The map shows each car as its photo in a ring: green moving (the arrow is its heading), yellow engine on, blue parked, orange not reporting. The list beside it has every car with its renter, booking, when it is due back (late in red) and its state.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press a car on the map or in the list for its card: last report, odometer, fuel, tracker battery, whether the tracker has the car&#39;s power, and the trip under way.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Alerts</b>: speeding, left Ontario, left your zone, still driving after the return time, low tracker battery, unplugged and not reporting. Each also comes to the bell and, with phone alerts on, under Urgent alerts. Press <b class="gd-ui">Show</b> to see where, <b class="gd-ui">Seen</b> when it is handled, or <b class="gd-ui">Mark all as seen</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Trips by booking</b>: each booking&#39;s trips, kilometres and top speed (red at the speeding level). Press the last trip to draw its route on the map.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-pair-a-tracker-with-a-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Pair a tracker with a car</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A new tracker that reports shows under <b class="gd-ui">Trackers</b>, &quot;Reporting, not on a car yet&quot;. Press <b class="gd-ui">Pair</b>, choose the car and the install date.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Or press <b class="gd-ui">Pair a tracker</b> and type its device ID (the IMEI or serial number on the tracker).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The install date starts the Tracker Fee on the owner&#39;s invoice when the car has none yet. A replacement tracker keeps the car&#39;s first date; the old tracker is taken off by itself.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> takes a tracker off a car (tick &quot;faulty&quot; for a broken one). The Tracker Fee is not changed.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-tracking-settings" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Tracking settings</h2><p class="gd-p">Below the trackers: the speeding level (140 km/h), the minutes of grace after the return time (15), the low battery level (20%), the hours before &quot;not reporting&quot; (6), the Ontario alert, and one optional zone (a name, its centre and a radius in km). History keeps a moving car&#39;s position once a minute for 90 days, trips and alerts for 365 days (at most 365: the privacy policy keeps tracker data 12 months).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Demo mode (off): simulated cars drive the GTA&#39;s highways here and on the Live map, for a demonstration. Nothing is saved. Turn it off before the trackers go live.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Make the ingest key</b>: the relay or tracker service signs every batch of positions with it. It is shown once; making a new one stops the old one at once.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>The Live map shows the same cars with its Fleet layer (tick Fleet).</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-the-listing-pipeline" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The listing pipeline</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b>. A draft waiting for review shows Needs review.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each row shows the car, plate, state, photos and the work done on it so far.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Start a listing</b> to begin one for a car that has none.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Open a car to review it.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/listings</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/560"><img src="/guides/img/admin-09-listings-desktop-970819b6.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="560"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:53.5%;top:37%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:87.2%;top:21.1%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:32.6%;top:37%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-review-a-listing" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Review a listing</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Steps to go live shows four numbered steps: <b class="gd-ui">1 Photos</b> (how many of the required photos are in, 14 for most cars, 13 for a two-seater with no rear seats), <b class="gd-ui">2 Cover plates</b>, <b class="gd-ui">3 Review</b> and <b class="gd-ui">4 Live on the site</b>. Each says what it needs and has one button to where it is done; the step to do now is in red. A step that stopped (a photo edit or the copy) shows under them with <b class="gd-ui">Retry</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Similar cars on file lists possible duplicates. Press <b class="gd-ui">Not a duplicate</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Same car</b>. An open flag does not keep the car off the site; only Same car does.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The copy is written by itself from the car&#39;s facts and published when it passes the checks: nothing to type. To change a line, press Change; that field is then locked and kept by every new version.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Under Photos, each public photo shows its plate state: Plate not checked, Plate covered or No plate visible.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/listings/704abf3d-8905-443d-a157-d52769cf7449</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/1100"><img src="/guides/img/admin-10-listing-review-desktop-352745fd.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="1100"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:20.6%;top:16.6%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:86.1%;top:47.5%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:19.9%;top:100%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:74.9%;top:100%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-cover-the-licence-plate" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Cover the licence plate</h2><p class="gd-p">The plates are checked by themselves. Every photo is looked at by the vision model within the day&#39;s free AI share: a plate it finds is covered (the photo shows Covered automatically, with how sure it was), a photo with no plate is marked No plate visible (No plate seen automatically), and a photo it is not sure of stays Plate not checked for you. While photos wait, the Photos card says how many. A wrong decision: press <b class="gd-ui">Undo</b> on the photo (the photo as it was comes back, Plate not checked), or <b class="gd-ui">Not a plate: no plate visible</b> on a cover put where there is no plate.</p><p class="gd-p">To cover a plate yourself, press <b class="gd-ui">Cover the plate</b> on the photo. The editor opens right under it.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Check the box over the plate, or press <b class="gd-ui">Suggest the plate</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Drag over a plate to draw a box. Drag a box to move it, or its corner to resize it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Under Cover the plate with, keep <b class="gd-ui">The CARMA Ontario plate</b> (on a rear plate: the company&#39;s own Ontario plate CARMA, drawn in the photo&#39;s perspective and light) or <b class="gd-ui">Edit the front plate out</b> (on a front photo: the bumper is filled in, no box), or choose <b class="gd-ui">A CarmaCars plate</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Pixelation</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Blur</b>. Photos covered the old way are made again the new way by themselves.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the covered photo</b>. <b class="gd-ui">Clear the boxes</b> starts over.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">No plate in the shot? Press <b class="gd-ui">No plate visible on this photo</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/listings/704abf3d-8905-443d-a157-d52769cf7449</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:690/703"><img src="/guides/img/admin-11-plate-editor-desktop-4219ad93.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="690" height="703"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:42.5%;top:83.8%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:49.6%;top:29.9%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:4.3%;top:77.4%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:15.5%;top:83.8%" aria-hidden="true">4</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:18.1%;top:91.2%" aria-hidden="true">5</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>The covered photo replaces the public one; the original is kept privately. Keyboard: N adds a box, the arrows move it, Shift and the arrows resize it, Delete removes it.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-publish" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Publish</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A real car that is not on the site is a line on To do: press <b class="gd-ui">Set rates and publish</b>. The daily rate is filled in (the car&#39;s own, or the suggested rate from similar cars or the class); change it if you like and press <b class="gd-ui">Publish now</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">On the car itself, the Listing tab has <b class="gd-ui">Publish now</b>; each open item of its checklist has a button to where it is done.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">From a listing review: press <b class="gd-ui">Approve and publish</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Approve, publish later</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Send back</b> with what to fix.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>The plate check never holds a car back: a real photo whose plate is not checked stays private (the other photos, or the sample photos, show instead) and goes public by itself once its plate is covered or marked not visible. Listings already live show &quot;Plate not checked&quot; on such photos.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-photos-filed-under-the-wrong-shot-and-interior-windows" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Photos filed under the wrong shot, and interior windows</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On the Photos card, each shot lists its photos. A photo filed under the wrong shot: press <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> under it, then <b class="gd-ui">Remove it</b>. The shot is free again: take or pick the right photo. The removed photo is kept privately and the removal is in the history. A live listing&#39;s photos change in the review instead (Reject).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Dashboard and seat photos: what shows through the windows is replaced by the studio background when the cut is clean (a quality check: some but not most of the frame seen through, high in the frame, a few clean regions, sharp edges). Otherwise the windows are blurred, and the photo is marked windows blurred. Nothing to do.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A car with 2 seats or fewer needs no Rear seats photo.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-a-listing-without-photos-yet-sample-photos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A listing without photos yet: sample photos</h2><p class="gd-p">A car can be listed before its photos are taken. Until then the site shows a sample photo.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Submit the listing without photos. The listing copy is still written for you from the car&#39;s details.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The car page and the car&#39;s card show a sample photo, captioned &quot;Sample photo&quot;, so renters know it is not this car. Staff see &quot;Using sample photos&quot; on the car and in Listings.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Publishing does not wait for a plate check: a sample photo has no plate.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Add the real photos when they are taken. Once real photos are approved they replace the sample at once; nothing else to do.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-sample-photos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Sample photos</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Sample photos</b>. The pictures a car shows until its real photos are in.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Every body type has a built-in picture (sedan, SUV, truck, van, coupe, hatchback, electric car).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Add your own: choose the Body type, and a Make and Model if the photo is of that exact model, pick the Photo, and press <b class="gd-ui">Add the photo</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The most specific photo wins: make and model, then make and body type, then body type. <b class="gd-ui">Turn off</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Delete</b> a photo you no longer want.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Cars using sample photos lists the cars still waiting for real photos. Each real car showing sample photos is also a line on To do, with <b class="gd-ui">Add photos</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/settings/sample-photos</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/812"><img src="/guides/img/admin-36-sample-photos-desktop-55c64070.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="812"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:26.8%;top:28.9%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-publish-now-and-new-cars-published-by-themselves" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Publish now, and new cars published by themselves</h2><p class="gd-p">Nothing between a new car and the site has to be finished first: the car goes on the site, and what is still open shows on its checklist.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Publish new cars automatically</b> (on by default): a new real car goes on the site by itself as soon as it has its year, make and model and its rates, when it is added with rates, when its rates are saved, when it is added for an owner, or when an owner&#39;s application is approved.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Otherwise open the car: its Listing tab says why it is not on the site and has <b class="gd-ui">Publish now</b>. A car with no rates yet is published with the suggested rates (similar cars, else the class defaults in Program settings); change them later on the Rates tab.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Every real car has its listing from the moment it is added, as a draft. It shows in Listings and in Not on the site yet until it is published.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">An owner&#39;s own application waits for your decision before its car is published by itself; Publish now still works.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">A car taken off the site by staff, or scheduled for a later date, is never published by itself: press <b class="gd-ui">Publish now</b>.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-the-checklist-what-is-still-open-on-a-listed-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The checklist: what is still open on a listed car</h2><p class="gd-p">Open items never stop publishing. They show as warnings on the car&#39;s Listing tab and after Publish now.</p><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Item</th><th scope="col">What it means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Paperwork</td><td>Ownership permit, registry forms, agreements signed, Forms C and D, upfront payment, registry visit, tracker, safety certificate</td></tr><tr><td>Insurance</td><td>Not on the fleet insurance policy yet: the car can be booked, but not handed over</td></tr><tr><td>Details</td><td>Colour, body, seats, gearbox: the car page leaves out what is missing</td></tr><tr><td>Photos</td><td>No real photos: sample photos stand in. A photo whose plate is not checked stays private until it is</td></tr><tr><td>No VIN yet</td><td>A car added by its plate alone: add the VIN when you have it</td></tr><tr><td>Possible duplicate</td><td>An open flag in Similar cars. Only Same car keeps the car off the site</td></tr><tr><td>Owner terms</td><td>The management fee (Revenue Share) and fees not set: a request uses the owner&#39;s terms or the standard grid</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-the-fleet-policy-rule-at-handover" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The fleet policy rule at handover</h2><p class="gd-p">A program owner&#39;s car is listed and can be requested, offered and paid for while its paperwork is open. It is never handed over until the insurer confirms in writing that it is on the fleet insurance policy.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Staff see a warning on a request and an offer for a car not on the policy yet.</li><li>The handover refuses the car until the insurer&#39;s confirmation is recorded (Owners and onboarding). The field app says so on the job.</li><li>Only real states keep a car off the site: retired, left the program, out of service, Turo only, bookings turned off, a self-managed owner in arrears, or a paused listing.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-cars-on-sample-photos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Cars on sample photos</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b> ends with <b class="gd-ui">Cars on sample photos</b>: each real car whose page still shows sample photos, with its newest handover photos (the check-in and check-out photos field staff take).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Where a handover photographed the car, press <b class="gd-ui">Use the handover photos</b>. They go into the car&#39;s listing as if taken on the capture screen.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">When every required shot is there, the listing is submitted: the studio editor puts the car on the CarmaCars backdrop, then the listing waits for your review like any other.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A car with no handover photos yet gets them at its next handover, or press <b class="gd-ui">Start a listing</b> and take them.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>The studio editor uses Cloudflare image transformations (5,000 a month included). Settings &gt; Usage counts them.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-a-car-s-registration-and-documents" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A car&#39;s registration and documents</h2><p class="gd-p">Open the car, then <b class="gd-ui">Owner &amp; documents</b>. The <b class="gd-ui">Registration</b> card:</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Correct the <b class="gd-ui">VIN</b> (it is checked: 17 characters, the check digit, not on another car; decoded again for the body style and trim), the <b class="gd-ui">Year</b> and the <b class="gd-ui">Body style</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Type the <b class="gd-ui">Ontario permit number</b> and the date the <b class="gd-ui">Plate sticker expires</b>. Fleet gets a task 30 days and 7 days before; save the new date after the renewal and the task closes.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Under <b class="gd-ui">Documents</b>, choose the kind (<b class="gd-ui">Ownership permit</b>, Safety Standards Certificate, owner&#39;s insurance, other), pick the photo or PDF and press <b class="gd-ui">Upload</b>. The ownership permit clears that item of the owner&#39;s checklist.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">For the <b class="gd-ui">Safety Standards Certificate</b>, also type its number, the date it was issued and the date it expires. Fleet gets a task 30 days and 7 days before it expires; upload the new certificate with its dates and the task closes. It is a document on the car, not a service record, and nothing is billed to the owner.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Add a car</b> takes the ownership permit and the Safety Standards Certificate too, under <b class="gd-ui">Documents (optional)</b>.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-a-car-added-under-the-wrong-owner" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A car added under the wrong owner</h2><p class="gd-p">Open the car, Overview, <b class="gd-ui">Who supplies the car</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Move to another owner</b>. Choose the owner, or <b class="gd-ui">CarmaCars (owner not known yet)</b>: the car becomes a company car, with no owner schedule or terms.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>The car&#39;s unsigned owner application and vehicle schedule are withdrawn (kept in the history), and its draft owner invoices are deleted. Nobody is notified.</li><li>It is refused once anything for the car is signed, issued, paid or on a statement.</li></ul><h3 class="gd-h3">The VIN from the car, not typed</h3><p class="gd-p">Every VIN field (Add a car, Add a car for an owner, the car&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Registration</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Start a listing</b>) has <b class="gd-ui">Scan the barcode</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Photo of the VIN</b>. Scan the barcode in the driver&#39;s door frame or at the bottom of the windshield: the phone&#39;s camera reads it by itself. Or take a photo of the VIN plate or sticker: the barcode in it is read first, else the photo is read for the printed VIN. The VIN is checked (17 characters, the check digit; I, O and Q become 1 and 0) and decoded as when you type it. Check it against the car before saving.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">Photos in any order</h3><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Add photos</b> on the listing takes any number of photos at once from the camera roll. Each is sorted to its shot by itself (front three-quarter, sides, rear, dashboard, seats and the rest); a shot that already has its photo sends the new one to the extra photos, so nothing is replaced by accident. The shots are a guide, not a rule: a listing is complete with 10 photos that can go on the site and one outside photo for the cover. Outside photos get the studio background: the car is cropped to its edges and placed big in the frame with its wheels on the floor and a soft shadow under the tyres, and any corner watermark or caption beside the car is left out. Inside and detail photos are kept as taken; when one has a watermark, a logo or caption text on it, the edge with the mark is cut off by itself, and a photo whose mark cannot be cut off (one in the middle) stays off the site until you replace it. <b class="gd-ui">Cover the plate</b> opens on every outside photo with the plate box suggested; check it and save.</p><p class="gd-p">Outside photos made before the newest framing (the car small in the frame, or without the model&#39;s name behind it) are made again with <b class="gd-ui">Frame the outside photos again</b> above the photos of the listing, then <b class="gd-ui">Yes, frame again</b>. The cover and the main outside views get the model&#39;s name lettered behind the car, as on the sample photos (for example CLA, C CLASS, AMG GT). The photos leave the site until their plates are checked again: the plate box is suggested on the new photos; check each and cover it. On a published listing each goes back on the site once its plate is checked.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-showroom-photos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Showroom photos</h2><p class="gd-p">Outside photos go in the CarmaCars showroom by themselves. When a real photographed room is stored (dealership or studio photos licensed for commercial use, fetched once from Wikimedia Commons with their author and licence kept), the car stands in it: about 70% of the width, its wheels on the room&#39;s floor, a soft shadow and a faint reflection under it, its light matched to the room, and no sign or lettering on the real wall. Program settings &gt; Listings has the switch (Photographed showroom rooms, on), the car&#39;s width and the cut-out quality floor: a cut-out that is not clean enough (pieces, a blurry or ragged edge) is never placed in a room, the real photo is used instead (its plate covered as usual) and the photo says so. Without a stored room it is the drawn dark showroom: a simple dark dealership with linear lights in the ceiling, a slatted wood wall between two light strips with a big lit CarmaCars sign, and a polished dark floor with the car&#39;s reflection and a shadow under each tyre. Every angle of a car is in the same room, and the cover has the model&#39;s name in metal letters on the wall under the sign. The image model may relight the car or turn it slightly; a photo that shows another car, model or colour is not used. <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b> has the switch (Showroom photos, on), the image model that makes the photos look photographed, and its daily limit. Past the limit, or when the image model is not available, the site makes the showroom itself for free, and the photo says why under it.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>A car whose photos were made on the black studio: press <b class="gd-ui">Apply showroom to this car</b> above its photos, then <b class="gd-ui">Yes, apply</b>.</li><li>Every car at once: <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Showroom photos</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Apply showroom to every car</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Yes, every car</b>.</li><li>Under a photo in the showroom: <b class="gd-ui">Redo</b> makes it again, <b class="gd-ui">Back to the original</b> puts back the version before the showroom.</li></ul><p class="gd-p">A car that stays where it was keeps its plate check. When the image model made the photo, check the plate again: the photo is off the site until you do. Photos made in the first showroom are made again in the new one with <b class="gd-ui">Apply showroom to this car</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Apply showroom to every car</b>.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-failed-photos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Failed photos</h2><p class="gd-p">The site makes the photo sizes itself: the image service is asked only to cut the car out (<b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b>: the switch to let the image service make every photo step is off). When the image service is busy or over its allowance, the photo still goes on the site from the original and is made again later. A listing marked Failed has <b class="gd-ui">Retry failed photos</b> in its note; <b class="gd-ui">Retry failed photos</b> at the top does every listing. They are made again a few at a time, and the listing leaves Failed when they are done.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-the-first-photo-plain-with-a-model-or-a-flyer" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The first photo: plain, with a model, or a flyer</h2><p class="gd-p">On a listing, under <b class="gd-ui">First photo</b>, choose what shows first on the site and in the Marketplace kit. Switch any time; the other photos stay as they are.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">Plain car</b>: the cover photo as it is (the default).</li><li><b class="gd-ui">With a model</b>: a car-show photo made by the image model, with a fully clothed adult model beside the car. It needs the image model; until it is made (or when the image model is not there) the plain cover shows, and the listing says why.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Flyer</b>: the cover photo with a band like a printed flyer: the car, the price a day from its live rates, the call to action, a badge and the logo. When the price, the words or the cover photo change, it is made again by itself within 10 minutes; the plain cover shows meanwhile.</li></ul><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Make it again</b> makes the chosen one again. The words of the flyer and the description of the model are in <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b> (First photo &quot;flyer&quot; and First photo &quot;with a model&quot;); {car}, {price}, {weekly} and {monthly} are filled for each car.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-marketing-photos-in-other-scenes" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Marketing photos in other scenes</h2><p class="gd-p">For Marketplace and social posts, a car&#39;s outside photos can be made again in other scenes. The website keeps its own photos in the dark showroom: a marketing set never replaces them.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On a listing, under <b class="gd-ui">Marketing photos</b>, choose a scene, or <b class="gd-ui">Mix: a different scene on each photo</b>, and press <b class="gd-ui">Make the marketing set</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The copies show as they are made. The dark showroom and the plain white studio are made by the site when the image model is not there; the photographic scenes (a bright showroom, a city street at night, the Toronto waterfront, a parking garage, Highway, a scenic road, Brick building) need the image model, and say so on the copy when it is not there.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Download (ZIP)</b> takes the set; the Marketplace kit&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">With scenes (ZIP)</b> takes the same set.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Marketing scenes</b> lists the scenes. A scene made in a real place has a photo of that place: Brick building picks its photo by itself: the widest outside photo, as taken, of the shareholders&#39; own cars. To use another, press <b class="gd-ui">Change the reference photo</b> and pick one (the shareholders&#39; cars&#39; photos come first), or upload one. The scenes&#39; names and words are in the <b class="gd-ui">Marketing scenes</b> setting.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-extra-photos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Extra photos</h2><p class="gd-p">A photo that fits no shot is an extra photo. Under the shots, <b class="gd-ui">Extra outside photos</b> (put on the studio background) and <b class="gd-ui">Extra inside and detail photos</b> (touched up) each take any number at once. They count toward the 10 photos, get the same plate check, and come after the standard shots on the car&#39;s page.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">In the review, <b class="gd-ui">Extra photos, in their order on the car page</b> lists them.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Drag a photo by its handle (⋮⋮), or press <b class="gd-ui">Earlier</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Later</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the order</b>.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-fix-a-cut-out" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Fix a cut-out</h2><p class="gd-p">When the background removal cuts badly (a mirror or a wheel missing, background left beside the car), press <b class="gd-ui">Edit the cut-out</b> under the outside photo.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Cut-out</b> shows the car over the photo as taken, shown faintly. Choose <b class="gd-ui">Erase</b> and brush over what should go, or <b class="gd-ui">Restore</b> and brush over what the cut-out took off. Set <b class="gd-ui">Brush size</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Zoom</b>; when zoomed, <b class="gd-ui">Move the view</b> pans. <b class="gd-ui">Undo</b> takes back the last stroke.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">On the studio</b> shows the car on the studio background. Drag the car to move it and use <b class="gd-ui">Size</b> to make it larger or smaller. <b class="gd-ui">Centre and full size</b> puts it back.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save as a new version</b>. The photo is made again in about a minute; the version before and the photo as taken are kept. <b class="gd-ui">Reset to the automatic cut-out</b> starts again from the automatic one.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>If the car did not move, the plate check carries over: a photo marked no plate visible stays so, and a covered plate is covered again on the new photo when the review is open. If the car moved, check the plate again. A photo made before cut-outs were kept shows <b class="gd-ui">Make the cut-out</b> first; the editor opens by itself when it is ready.</div></aside><p class="gd-p">Every photo also gets a light touch-up by itself (exposure, levels, a little contrast and colour, mild sharpening), never enough to change the paint colour or hide a scratch. Turn it off for one photo with <b class="gd-ui">Use original colours</b> under it (the photo is made again; approve it again), or for every photo in Admin &gt; Settings &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> (Listings) with <b class="gd-ui">Auto-enhance listing photos</b>. The photo as uploaded is always kept.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-import-photos-from-a-google-drive-link" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Import photos from a Google Drive link</h2><p class="gd-p">The owner often hands over a car&#39;s photos as a public Google Drive folder, or one big folder with a folder per make and then per car. You do not download them: paste the link.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">One car.</b> On the car&#39;s listing, under the capture, <b class="gd-ui">Import photos from a Google Drive link</b>. Paste the folder link (shared with Anyone with the link) and press <b class="gd-ui">Import the photos</b>. Every photo in the folder, and in the folders inside it, is added to this car as if you had pressed Add photos: each is sorted to its shot (else filed as an extra photo, in file-name order), put on the studio background and checked for its plate. The box under the link, <b class="gd-ui">Submit the listing for processing when its photos are in</b>, is on by default.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Many cars.</b> <b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Import photos from Drive</b> (a button on Vehicles). Paste the top folder&#39;s link and press <b class="gd-ui">Read the folder</b>. The page walks every folder and proposes a car for each folder that holds photos, from the year, make, model, colour and plate in the folder names (the make folder above counts; 01 Motors partner cars come first). Check the table: tick or untick <b class="gd-ui">Import</b>, change the car in the list (the likely cars come first), leave out a folder with <b class="gd-ui">Do not import this folder</b>. A line marked <b class="gd-ui">Check this one</b> matched two alike cars. Then press <b class="gd-ui">Import N photos from M folders</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The page follows the import by itself. You can leave it and come back: it runs in the background.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The end shows the summary: imported, skipped and failed, and why for each (a file over 15 MB, a file that is not a photo, the same photo already on the car, a folder not shared).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Try the failed photos again</b> takes only the ones that failed. Pressing Import on the same link again never adds a photo twice: a Drive file already on the car is skipped, and so is the same picture under another name. A photo you took off the car can be imported again.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>JPG, PNG, HEIC and WebP only (HEIC and WebP are made JPEG first). At most 15 MB a photo, 600 photos, 400 folders and 4 GB in one import. Drive is asked politely, one photo at a time; a big import takes a while.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Without a key, Drive shows only the first 50 files of a folder on its public page; a folder with more is read in full when Drive allows it. In <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Photo import from Google Drive</b> box takes a Google API key with the Drive API on (after it is saved only its last 4 characters are shown, and it is never written to the change log): with it, folders of any size are read and photos download without Drive&#39;s warning pages.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-test-bookings-and-deleting-a-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Test bookings and deleting a car</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On a booking made only to try the site, press <b class="gd-ui">Mark as a test booking</b> (Admins only; the reason is optional). <b class="gd-ui">Make it a real booking again</b> undoes it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">A car whose bookings are all test bookings can be deleted: the test bookings and their test payments go with it, and a copy is kept in the archive of deleted requests.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A car with a real booking cannot be deleted.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-pickup-from-owner-and-return-to-owner-release-28" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Pickup from owner and return to owner (release 28)</h2><p class="gd-p">On a car&#39;s page, <b class="gd-ui">Pickup from owner and return to owner</b> records the car&#39;s condition when CarmaCars picks it up from its owner or gives it back: the date and time, km, fuel, many photos at once with the suggested angles, and notes. <b class="gd-ui">Add photos</b> adds more to a record later. The owner sees these records read only on the car&#39;s page in their portal. They are the baseline condition for any dispute.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-incident-cards-release-34" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Incident cards (release 34)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Vehicles</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Incident cards</b> prints the card for each car: what to do in an accident or a breakdown, the support number from Settings, a roadside number when there is one, a QR code to report it in the app, and the fleet insurance slip. Open a car and press <b class="gd-ui">Incident card</b> to print only that car; on the list, <b class="gd-ui">Print all cars</b> prints them all, two cards to a Letter page with crop marks, ready to laminate. Under Fleet insurance policy press <b class="gd-ui">Add the policy</b> (the insurer, the policy number, the dates, the named insured, the roadside number on the slip) and choose the uploaded slip if you have one: it is printed as it is, otherwise the fields are. The card never shows a premium. Fleet staff print the same cards from their portal.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-field-jobs-shifts-and-who-gets-a-job" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Field jobs, shifts and who gets a job</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Field jobs</b>, is the board Fleet uses, with every action Fleet has. Field staff take shifts you publish with <b class="gd-ui">Publish shifts</b>. Jobs go on shifts, not on people: each job is put on the shift covering its time (or that day&#39;s), whoever holds the shift does it (several people share the jobs, least busy first), a shift nobody holds keeps its jobs for whoever claims it, and work lands only on days with shifts (work due on a day without shifts moves to the day before, or to the next day with shifts when it comes in on the day; the booking&#39;s own times never change). A booking whose handover or return falls on a day with no shifts shows a warning on the board and on the booking. <b class="gd-ui">To a shift</b> moves a job to another shift. You can give a job to a field person on a shift that day or to an Admin, take it off with <b class="gd-ui">Unassign</b> (tick <b class="gd-ui">Tell them</b> to let them know), and an Admin who holds a job opens it on the field portal. A person who has not passed the academy cannot be given a job or take a shift. A shift with jobs and nobody on it within 24 hours alerts Fleet and the Admins once.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('va', 'fleet', 'chapter', 'finance', 'You keep the cars moving: field jobs, daily checks, photo reviews after returns, and the listings with their duplicate check and plate covering. There is no commission for Fleet, but your help is credited on the booking (Helped by) and on your scorecard.

Your rail: Queue, Today, Field jobs, Field hours, Daily checks, Photo reviews, Calendar, Listings, Similar cars, Find a renter and Scorecard.

## Schedule field jobs

Every confirmed booking gets its handover (or delivery) and return (or pickup) jobs by itself, at the booking''s times and place, and put on a shift: the shift covering its time, or that day''s (see Shifts and who gets a job). The people on the shift share its jobs, least busy first. You check and change them.

1. Jobs, next three days: each with its place, its shift, its field staff and whether they acknowledged it. "Made from the booking" marks the ones made by themselves; when the booking moves, they move too, unless you changed them.
2. Change a job with **To a shift** (another shift), **Assign** or **Reassign** (a field person on a shift that day when the day has shifts, or an Admin), **Move** (time and place) or **Cancel**.
3. Handovers and returns without a job (when the automatic jobs are off, or one was cancelled) are listed first: press **Schedule**, the place filled in from the booking.
4. An Admin turns the automatic jobs or the assignment off in Settings > Program.

![](/guides/img/va-fleet-02-field-jobs-desktop-8e721230.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 565; address: carmacars.ca/va/fleet; pins: 1 17.9 51.3")

## Shifts and who gets a job

Field staff take their shifts from a schedule you publish, ideally a week ahead. A job is given by itself only to a field person who passed the academy and holds a shift that day, and work lands only on days with shifts.

1. On **Field jobs**, **Shifts, next seven days** shows each day and how many people are on a shift, and each shift its jobs (**Jobs on it**). A shift with jobs and nobody on it is marked; within 24 hours of its start you get an alert and a To do, once.
2. Press **Publish shifts**: the first day''s start and end, how many people, and for how many days the same hours repeat. Field staff take them on their phones.
3. **Add a person** puts someone on a shift and **Remove** takes them off. A person who has not passed the academy cannot take shifts or be given a job.
4. A shift nobody claimed keeps its jobs: field staff see them when they look for shifts to claim, and the one who claims it gets them. A shift given up or swapped takes its jobs along; a cancelled shift sends them to another shift.
5. Work due on a day with no shifts moves to the day before when it is known in advance, or to the next day with shifts when it comes in on the day. The job shows its planned day and keeps the booking''s real time; the renter''s times never change. A booking whose handover or return falls on a day with no shifts shows a warning: cover it, or move the booking time.
6. **Unassign** takes a job off its person and its shift; tick **Tell them** only if they should know. The Admins can be given a job too (no shift needed).

## Fleet map

At the top of **Field jobs**: every car on the map with its renter, booking, due-back time and state, the alerts, and the trips by booking, the same as the Admin''s. Only Admins and fleet staff see positions.

1. Press a car for its card: last report, odometer, fuel, tracker battery and the trip under way.
2. An alert (speeding, left Ontario or the zone, still driving after the return time, low or unplugged tracker, not reporting) also comes to your bell and as an urgent phone alert. Call the renter, then press **Seen**.
3. A car still driving after its return time: call, send the late notice and offer a paid extension, as for any late return.

## Field hours

Field staff clock in and out on their phones. You see who is clocked in and every shift of the two-week pay period, and you fix what they cannot.

1. Open **Field hours**. **Clocked in now** lists who is on, since when. **Earlier period** and **Later period** move between pay periods.
2. Someone forgot to clock out: press **Clock out for them**, set the time they finished and write the reason.
3. Someone forgot to clock in, or a time is wrong: **Add hours** enters a shift, **Change** fixes one and **Remove** takes one out. Each needs a reason; the change is kept in a log with what it was before.
4. Once an Admin approves the pay run of a period, its shifts are locked: ask the Admin. You see hours only, not rates or pay.

### Where they clocked in
The hours list shows where each person clocked in and out: a map link and the distance from the lot. A clock in or out over 500 m away, or with the location refused, is shown in bold with the reason the person wrote. Their location is asked only at those two moments, never in between.

## Daily checks

Twice a day: the opening check by 9:00 and the closing check by 18:00.

1. Open **Daily checks** and choose **Opening check** or **Closing check**.
2. Each line shows what was found. Tick OK, or Problem with a note.
3. Press **Save the opening check** (or **Save the closing check**). You can save it again.

![](/guides/img/va-fleet-03-daily-checks-desktop-be06d6c0.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 820; address: carmacars.ca/va/checks; pins: 1 6.5 15.4, 2 44.7 42.0, 3 64.2 94.0")

## Check a car out or in

Fleet, Sales and Customer service check cars out and in from the booking.

1. On a confirmed booking press **Check in (pickup)**; on a booking on rent, **Check out (return)**. Today lists the ones due, each with its button.
2. The checklist field staff use opens: readings (km and fuel or charge), the photo set with the plate and the gauges, damage close-ups and both signatures.
3. Afterwards press **Photo report**: times, Late by, kilometres, fuel, photos and the return charges. Fleet waives a charge with **Waive** and a reason.

## Photo reviews after a return

After each return, the field photo set waits under **Photo reviews**. Compare it with the pickup set. Press **Review done**, or **Ask for a re-shoot** if a photo is missing or unclear.

## Similar cars

A possible duplicate never keeps a car off the site: it shows on the car''s checklist until you decide. Only Same car takes it off.

1. Each flag shows the car, what it looks like (same VIN, plate, photo or specs) and the other car.
2. Compare the permit, the plate and the photos.
3. Press **Not a duplicate** with a note when they are different cars, or **Same car** when they are.

![](/guides/img/va-fleet-06-similar-cars-desktop-562b0382.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 460; address: carmacars.ca/va/similar-cars; pins: 1 23.6 30.4, 3 94.8 30.4")

## Rates and kilometres

From a listing, press **The car and its rates**, or open the car from Field jobs and its **Rates & fees** tab.

1. Type the rates an Admin set. Only the daily rate is needed; the others follow from it when empty. The weekend rate is a price per day for each day that starts on a Friday or Saturday.
2. Keep **Use the defaults** for the kilometres, or choose **Custom for this car**.
3. Check What renters pay under the fields, then press **Save the rates**. Rates, kilometres and deposit save together.
4. **Price limits**, below: the lowest and highest daily rate the owner accepts, read only. Offers, promo codes and lead-time pricing stay between them; an Admin or the owner changes them, and only an Admin allows one booking outside them.

## Listings and covering plates

1. Open **Listings**. A draft waiting shows Needs review. Open it.
2. The copy is written by itself (change a line only if you must: it is then kept). Check the photos: on each public photo, cover the plate or mark it not visible.

![](/guides/img/va-fleet-05-listings-desktop-d2672e0a.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 340; address: carmacars.ca/va/listings; pins: 1 54.5 49.1")

3. The listing''s Steps to go live says what is next: 1 Photos, 2 Cover plates, 3 Review, 4 Live on the site, each with its button. The plate box is suggested by itself on every outside photo as the listing opens (Box suggested). Press **Cover the plate** and check it; **Suggest the plate** asks again. A photo filed under the wrong shot: **Remove** under it on the Photos card, then take the right one.
4. Drag over a plate to draw a box; drag a box to move it, its corner to resize it.
5. Keep **The CARMA Ontario plate** on a rear plate or **Edit the front plate out** on a front photo (or choose **A CarmaCars plate**, **Pixelation** or **Blur**), then **Save the covered photo**.
6. No plate in the shot? **No plate visible on this photo**.

![](/guides/img/admin-11-plate-editor-phone-95d5afd2.jpg "phone; size: 390 776; pins: 3 52.6 78.9, 4 50.0 43.8, 5 61.5 62.1, 6 43.1 92.3")

> Watch out: The plate check never holds a car back: a photo whose plate is not checked stays private, and goes public by itself once it is covered or marked. The covered photo replaces the public one; the original is kept privately.

## Missing angles and short videos

On a listing, below First photo (Sales: in the Marketplace kit of the car).

1. A required angle with no photo? Fleet and Sales press **Make** and the angle (for example **Make Rear**): the image model makes the view from the car''s photos, within its free daily use. Check it is the same car, then **Approve** or **Reject**.
2. Press **Make a short video** for a 9:16 video of the car''s approved photos with the price and the call to action. Keep the tab in front until it says Saved, then **Download** it or schedule it on your Marketing page (Scheduled posts).

> Watch out: An AI view shows on the site after the real photos, labelled AI view. It is never the cover and never damage or condition evidence. A real photo always replaces it.

## Publish now

Customer service and fleet publish a car themselves; nothing has to be finished first.

1. Open the car from Listings or Field jobs. Its listing says why it is not on the site yet; press **Publish now**. With no rates yet it uses the suggested rates (similar cars, else the class defaults).
2. What is still open (paperwork, details, photos, No VIN yet for a car added by its plate, a possible duplicate) shows as warnings after Publish now and on the car. None of them stops publishing.
3. New cars with their rates usually go on the site by themselves (Publish new cars automatically, on by default). A car taken off the site by staff waits for Publish now.

> Tip: A car not on the fleet insurance policy yet can be requested, offered and paid for, but never handed over until the insurer confirms it. Requests and offers for such a car show a warning.

## Calendar sync with Turo and other platforms

**Cars** > **Calendar sync**: a car listed on Turo or Getaround must never be booked twice.

1. Turo has no calendar link: Turo''s trip emails come in by themselves, find their car by themselves (Turo car number, plate, VIN, year, make, model, trim, colour, what earlier emails taught) and block it with the turnaround. Nothing to set up per car.
2. An email the reader cannot place waits as "Which car is this?": press **Which car is this?** and press the right car (best guesses first). It is remembered for that car''s next emails. If the dates or trip number are missing: **Add as a Turo trip** (choose the car, check the dates) or **Dismiss**. A trip whose email did not come: **Add a Turo trip** on the car.
3. Each Turo trip shows the guest''s name and phone when Turo''s email includes them. Contact a Turo guest only about their trip, never with promotions.
4. Turo cannot read our calendar: under "Block on Turo", block each CarmaCars booking on the car''s Turo calendar, then press **Done on Turo**. Dates that changed or a booking cancelled here show the dates to free on Turo.
5. Getaround, Google Calendar or another platform with a calendar (iCal) link: open **Add a calendar link**, choose the platform, paste it and press **Add the link**. Copy the car''s CarmaCars link for that platform with **Copy** and paste it into the platform''s calendar import.
6. A double booking raises an urgent task for you and an email: move, swap or cancel one trip. A link that stops working raises a task after 3 failed reads: copy it from the platform again.

### Add the photos and readings
A pickup or return recorded with the details later gives Fleet the task **Add the photos and readings for CC-...**. Open the booking and press **Add the check-in (or check-out) photos and readings**: the usual checklist opens without the ready check or the renter''s signature. Take the photos, the odometer, fuel, keys (and cleanliness at a return), sign and save. The task closes by itself; it cannot be closed by hand before.

## Bookings now

**Rentals** > **Bookings** opens on Now for fleet and customer service: the cars out with their renter and due-back countdown, coming back today and tomorrow (overdue first, in red), going out in the next 72 hours with what is ready, the money due in 7 days and the free cars. It refreshes by itself every 30 seconds. A booking listed as **Out (pickup not recorded)** left without a check-in: press **Mark picked up**, then add the photos, km and fuel from the task. A car overdue or due back today has **Returned** (here, on Today and at the top of the booking): give the return time (now, or earlier; the late charges follow it) and the km and fuel if known. The overdue messages stop and the task for the photos is yours. The search above it finds any booking.

### The renter says the car is back

An urgent To do "The renter says the car is back" means the renter pressed **I''ve returned the car** on an overdue booking. Their overdue notices are paused. Open the booking, check the car (place, tracker, the renter''s photos), then press **Confirm** (correct the odometer, fuel or time first if needed; the trip is completed) or **Deny** with the reason (the renter is told and the notices start again).

**Start a listing** takes the VIN from the car: **Scan the barcode** in the door frame or under the windshield, or **Photo of the VIN**.

**Add photos** on a listing takes any number of photos at once, in any order: each is sorted to its shot. A photo that fits no shot goes in with **Extra outside photos** or **Extra inside and detail photos**; drag the extras into their order in the review and press **Save the order**. 10 photos and one outside photo complete the listing. Outside photos are framed big on the studio floor with a shadow under the tyres; a watermark or caption at a photo''s edge is cut off by itself. **Cover the plate** opens with the plate box suggested: check it and save. A car small in the frame, or no model name behind it: press **Frame the outside photos again** (then check the plates again). A bad cut-out (a mirror missing, background left): press **Edit the cut-out**, erase or restore with the brush, move or size the car on the studio, then **Save as a new version**. The version before is kept; if the car did not move, the plate check carries over. Every photo gets a light touch-up by itself; tick **Use original colours** under a photo to make it again without it. Outside photos go in the CarmaCars showroom: a real photographed dealership room when one is stored (the car about 70% of the width, its wheels on the floor, a soft shadow and a faint reflection; no logo on a real wall), else the dark drawn showroom (the logo on the wall, the model''s name behind the car on the cover). A cut-out that is not clean enough is never placed in a room: the real photo is used instead (its plate covered as usual), noted on the photo. A car still on the black studio: press **Apply showroom to this car**; **Listings** > **Apply showroom to every car** does every car. Under a photo, **Redo** makes it again and **Back to the original** puts back the version before. **Marketing photos** on a listing makes copies in other scenes for Marketplace and social posts (choose a scene or **Mix: a different scene on each photo**, then **Make the marketing set**); the website''s photos stay as they are. **First photo** on a listing chooses what shows first on the site and in the Marketplace kit: **Plain car**, **With a model** (the image model''s car-show photo, a fully clothed adult model beside the car) or **Flyer** (the price a day from the live rates, the call to action and the logo on the cover). Switch any time; until the chosen one is made the plain cover shows.
## One screen, many photos (release 28)

**Import photos from a Google Drive link** on a listing adds the photos of a public Drive folder to the car, sorted and processed like Add photos. **Listings** > **Import photos from Drive** reads a whole folder of folders (one per make, then per car), proposes the car for each folder, and imports once you confirm the table. The page follows the import and ends with what was imported, skipped and failed, and why. The same Drive file is never added twice. Customer service can import into a car whose listing is already started; Fleet and Admin can start one.

Check-in and check-out are one screen on the booking page: the time, km, fuel, many photos at once (tag angles if you like) and a note. The renter''s own photos join the same report; each photo shows who took it. On a car''s page, record **Pickup from owner** and **Return to owner** with photos: the owner sees them.

## Repair costs on a car

On a car''s page, **Kickbacks and repairs** lists its repair costs and the kickbacks partners paid on it. **Add a repair cost**: the date, the shop or another vendor, what was done, the amount and tax, who paid (CarmaCars, the owner or the insurer), the claim and a photo or PDF of the receipt.

## When a check stops the pickup or the return (release 33)
On the booking page, **What stops the pickup now** (or the return) lists each check that stops it, in plain words. When the trip must go ahead anyway, press **Ask an Admin to override the pickup** (or the return), give the actual time, the km and fuel if you know them, and why. An Admin gets an alert and approves in one tap; the pickup (or the return) is then recorded with the time you entered, and the booking''s history says who asked and who approved. You can cancel your request while it waits. A trip that happened and was never recorded: **Ask to record a past trip** with both times; once an Admin approves, the booking lands in Returned so the deposit can be settled.

## Incident cards (release 34)
**Cars**, then **Incident cards**, prints the card for the visor or the glovebox: what to do in an accident or a breakdown, our support and roadside numbers, a QR code to report it in the app, and the fleet insurance slip. On a car''s page, **Incident card** prints that car; on the list, **Print all cars** prints every car, two cards to a Letter page with crop marks. Laminate it and put one in each car. The insurance policy on the card is set by an Admin; until it is, the card tells the renter to ask for the slip. No price is ever printed on it.

## Government forms (release 35)
The official ServiceOntario forms of each owner''s car are on the owner''s page and the car''s page, under **Government forms**. Open a form, press **Change a value**, choose the box, type the value and the reason, and **Save**: the form is made again as a new version, and the earlier versions stay under **Versions** with their downloads. **Back to the records** undoes a change. A form signed in ink or filed is never changed. **Make again** keeps the values changed by hand unless you tick **Discard the values changed by hand**. **Owners**, then **Government forms**, opens the forms'' mapping (which value goes in which box): preview it on a sample car, write what you changed and save; every save is kept under **Earlier mappings**. Only the boxes are filled: the form''s own text and layout never change.

## Odometer and fuel at every check-in and check-out

Every check-in and check-out on one screen asks for two photos besides the others:

1. **Photo of the dashboard**: the odometer and the fuel gauge, from the camera roll or the camera. The site reads it and asks, for example, "Odometer 45,210 km, fuel 3/4: correct?". Press **Yes, correct**, or **No, I will type it** and type the odometer and pick the fuel in eighths.
2. **Selfie in front of the car**: taken now with the camera, never from the camera roll. A selfie without a fresh capture time is noted on the report for you to check; it never stops the check-in.

At the return the site compares with the pickup: km driven, km over the included allowance and the fuel difference. The extra km (the booking''s rate per km) are added to the booking by themselves. The fuel is prepared as a suggested line: the car''s tank x the fuel missing x the local pump price of its grade x 1.25, plus the $20 refuelling fee (an electric car: battery kWh x the charge missing x $0.40, plus the fee). You and Finance confirm it on the deposit review; no card is charged by it. The photo report shows both dashboard photos side by side with the readings and these charges.

## Change the car of a confirmed booking

A car with a problem before pickup? On the booking, press **Change the car**, choose a car free for the dates and say why. The price comes from the new car''s rate sheet; more to pay is left open for the renter, less becomes a refund for approval. The jobs move to the new car and the renter gets one email.

## An accident reported by a renter

A renter can report an accident from the accident card on their booking. It opens the incident with its first-response steps and your To do, and sends you an urgent alert (on duty) and to Admins: what happened, where, the photos and videos, the other party, the police report number, whether anyone is hurt and whether the car can be driven. Call the renter at once; a car that cannot be driven is already out of service with its calendar blocked.
## Payments and calls (release 35)
Fleet takes payments on a booking''s **Money** tab: text or email a pay link, charge the saved card when the renter agreed, hold the deposit, or record cash or an e-Transfer received (within your single limit; Finance gets a To do to check it). Refunds, captures and voids stay with Finance and the Admins.

Calls and texts about pickups, returns, deliveries and cars on rent come to Fleet first: the caller pop-up shows them, and **More fleet** > **Calls and texts** is your inbox. A car late back has **Returning now** on its late panel: press it when the renter says they are on the way, and they get no more overdue reminders for that return time.

The official ServiceOntario forms of each owner''s car are on the owner''s page and the car''s page, under **Government forms**. Open a form, press **Change a value**, choose the box, type the value and the reason, and **Save**: the form is made again as a new version, and the earlier versions stay under **Versions** with their downloads. **Back to the records** undoes a change. A form signed in ink or filed is never changed. **Make again** keeps the values changed by hand unless you tick **Discard the values changed by hand**. **Owners**, then **Government forms**, opens the forms'' mapping (which value goes in which box): preview it on a sample car, write what you changed and save; every save is kept under **Earlier mappings**. Only the boxes are filled: the form''s own text and layout never change. The owner signs each form on screen: the page shows **Owner''s signature** beside the form (who, when, the version) and **Download the print-ready form** has no signature on it. A value changed after signing shows **Changed since signed** and the owner is asked to sign again.

## Close ended trips

A back-dated close sends the renter no email or text. Fleet gets a To do when a trip is still open 2 hours after its return time, and the morning digest lists how many are open.

**Field jobs** > **Close ended trips**: tick the trips that ended and were never closed, mark them returned on time or late (with the time), choose the deposit decision (deduct the balance owed, deduct the late fee, or release in full) and press **Close**. An expired card hold is settled by expiry at once. An Admin presses Release for the rest. On a booking, an expired hold after the return has **Mark settled (released by expiry)**.

## Field applicant calls (release 35)

Field applicants who pass the AI interview book a 10-minute live call in the hour before the weekly townhall. **Field applicant calls** on your home page lists the six slots and who took each one.

## Value and fuel on the car page (release 35)

**Cars** > the car > **Overview** > **Value and fuel**:

- **Canadian Black Book value** (with the date checked) or an **Estimated value (when no Black Book)**: renters on credit card coverage are checked against it. With neither, they go to staff review.
- **Tank (litres)** and **Fuel grade** (regular, premium or diesel; empty uses the class), or **Battery (kWh)** for an electric car. Empty uses the default in Program settings.

Press **Save**. Customer service sees the card; only Fleet and an Admin change it.

## Shifts, delivery and fuel (release 35)

- The shift board shows each field person''s availability, the standing weekly shifts, who is under the minimum, and for each slot the people to ask. A shift nobody claimed 48 hours ahead alerts you.
- You can approve new staff at the fourth onboarding step, or reject with a reason.
- Delivery is priced by distance from 1570 Midland Ave; the fuel line at the return is a suggestion from the tank and the pump price for you to check on the deposit review.
- An Admin can delete a car that has only test bookings; a car with a real booking stays.

## Calls first, texts after (release 37)

Your main priority is always to be on the phone with people.

1. Answer a ringing call before anything else, and return a missed call at once.
2. **Call before you text.** On a lead, a renter or a booking, **Call** is the first button and **Text** the second.
3. A text is a follow-up: after a call attempt (no answer, a voicemail left), or when the person asked for a text.
4. On your To do and on **Unanswered**, missed calls and call-backs are listed above unanswered texts.

## A lead you handle on a call (release 37)

When you answer or place a call with a lead, add a note on it, or create it from a call, the lead is yours for a limited time (15 minutes, as a Sales claim; an Admin can change it in **Settings** > **Sales**). Every call you handle adds the time again.

- Sales see **Being handled by** your first name and your function with the time, on the lead and in every list. They cannot claim it, call, text or email it, or set an outcome meanwhile, and **Next lead** skips it.
- Another customer service or Fleet person can still work it; their call or note takes the hold over.
- When it ends, the lead goes back to the salesperson who had a claim on it or who brought it, else to the open list. An Admin can **Release hold** earlier.
- A booking made from the lead is credited as always: customer service and Fleet get no sales commission for it.
- Nobody who has not finished onboarding holds a lead.', 'Fleet', 'Field jobs, daily checks, photo reviews, similar cars and listings.',
  'You keep the cars moving: field jobs, daily checks, photo reviews after returns, and the listings with their duplicate check and plate covering. There is no commission for Fleet, but your help is credited on the booking (Helped by) and on your scorecard.

Your rail: Queue, Today, Field jobs, Field hours, Daily checks, Photo reviews, Calendar, Listings, Similar cars, Find a renter and Scorecard.

## Schedule field jobs

Every confirmed booking gets its handover (or delivery) and return (or pickup) jobs by itself, at the booking''s times and place, and put on a shift: the shift covering its time, or that day''s (see Shifts and who gets a job). The people on the shift share its jobs, least busy first. You check and change them.

1. Jobs, next three days: each with its place, its shift, its field staff and whether they acknowledged it. "Made from the booking" marks the ones made by themselves; when the booking moves, they move too, unless you changed them.
2. Change a job with **To a shift** (another shift), **Assign** or **Reassign** (a field person on a shift that day when the day has shifts, or an Admin), **Move** (time and place) or **Cancel**.
3. Handovers and returns without a job (when the automatic jobs are off, or one was cancelled) are listed first: press **Schedule**, the place filled in from the booking.
4. An Admin turns the automatic jobs or the assignment off in Settings > Program.

![](/guides/img/va-fleet-02-field-jobs-desktop-8e721230.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 565; address: carmacars.ca/va/fleet; pins: 1 17.9 51.3")

## Shifts and who gets a job

Field staff take their shifts from a schedule you publish, ideally a week ahead. A job is given by itself only to a field person who passed the academy and holds a shift that day, and work lands only on days with shifts.

1. On **Field jobs**, **Shifts, next seven days** shows each day and how many people are on a shift, and each shift its jobs (**Jobs on it**). A shift with jobs and nobody on it is marked; within 24 hours of its start you get an alert and a To do, once.
2. Press **Publish shifts**: the first day''s start and end, how many people, and for how many days the same hours repeat. Field staff take them on their phones.
3. **Add a person** puts someone on a shift and **Remove** takes them off. A person who has not passed the academy cannot take shifts or be given a job.
4. A shift nobody claimed keeps its jobs: field staff see them when they look for shifts to claim, and the one who claims it gets them. A shift given up or swapped takes its jobs along; a cancelled shift sends them to another shift.
5. Work due on a day with no shifts moves to the day before when it is known in advance, or to the next day with shifts when it comes in on the day. The job shows its planned day and keeps the booking''s real time; the renter''s times never change. A booking whose handover or return falls on a day with no shifts shows a warning: cover it, or move the booking time.
6. **Unassign** takes a job off its person and its shift; tick **Tell them** only if they should know. The Admins can be given a job too (no shift needed).

## Fleet map

At the top of **Field jobs**: every car on the map with its renter, booking, due-back time and state, the alerts, and the trips by booking, the same as the Admin''s. Only Admins and fleet staff see positions.

1. Press a car for its card: last report, odometer, fuel, tracker battery and the trip under way.
2. An alert (speeding, left Ontario or the zone, still driving after the return time, low or unplugged tracker, not reporting) also comes to your bell and as an urgent phone alert. Call the renter, then press **Seen**.
3. A car still driving after its return time: call, send the late notice and offer a paid extension, as for any late return.

## Field hours

Field staff clock in and out on their phones. You see who is clocked in and every shift of the two-week pay period, and you fix what they cannot.

1. Open **Field hours**. **Clocked in now** lists who is on, since when. **Earlier period** and **Later period** move between pay periods.
2. Someone forgot to clock out: press **Clock out for them**, set the time they finished and write the reason.
3. Someone forgot to clock in, or a time is wrong: **Add hours** enters a shift, **Change** fixes one and **Remove** takes one out. Each needs a reason; the change is kept in a log with what it was before.
4. Once an Admin approves the pay run of a period, its shifts are locked: ask the Admin. You see hours only, not rates or pay.

### Where they clocked in
The hours list shows where each person clocked in and out: a map link and the distance from the lot. A clock in or out over 500 m away, or with the location refused, is shown in bold with the reason the person wrote. Their location is asked only at those two moments, never in between.

## Daily checks

Twice a day: the opening check by 9:00 and the closing check by 18:00.

1. Open **Daily checks** and choose **Opening check** or **Closing check**.
2. Each line shows what was found. Tick OK, or Problem with a note.
3. Press **Save the opening check** (or **Save the closing check**). You can save it again.

![](/guides/img/va-fleet-03-daily-checks-desktop-be06d6c0.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 820; address: carmacars.ca/va/checks; pins: 1 6.5 15.4, 2 44.7 42.0, 3 64.2 94.0")

## Check a car out or in

Fleet, Sales and Customer service check cars out and in from the booking.

1. On a confirmed booking press **Check in (pickup)**; on a booking on rent, **Check out (return)**. Today lists the ones due, each with its button.
2. The checklist field staff use opens: readings (km and fuel or charge), the photo set with the plate and the gauges, damage close-ups and both signatures.
3. Afterwards press **Photo report**: times, Late by, kilometres, fuel, photos and the return charges. Fleet waives a charge with **Waive** and a reason.

## Photo reviews after a return

After each return, the field photo set waits under **Photo reviews**. Compare it with the pickup set. Press **Review done**, or **Ask for a re-shoot** if a photo is missing or unclear.

## Similar cars

A possible duplicate never keeps a car off the site: it shows on the car''s checklist until you decide. Only Same car takes it off.

1. Each flag shows the car, what it looks like (same VIN, plate, photo or specs) and the other car.
2. Compare the permit, the plate and the photos.
3. Press **Not a duplicate** with a note when they are different cars, or **Same car** when they are.

![](/guides/img/va-fleet-06-similar-cars-desktop-562b0382.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 460; address: carmacars.ca/va/similar-cars; pins: 1 23.6 30.4, 3 94.8 30.4")

## Rates and kilometres

From a listing, press **The car and its rates**, or open the car from Field jobs and its **Rates & fees** tab.

1. Type the rates an Admin set. Only the daily rate is needed; the others follow from it when empty. The weekend rate is a price per day for each day that starts on a Friday or Saturday.
2. Keep **Use the defaults** for the kilometres, or choose **Custom for this car**.
3. Check What renters pay under the fields, then press **Save the rates**. Rates, kilometres and deposit save together.
4. **Price limits**, below: the lowest and highest daily rate the owner accepts, read only. Offers, promo codes and lead-time pricing stay between them; an Admin or the owner changes them, and only an Admin allows one booking outside them.

## Listings and covering plates

1. Open **Listings**. A draft waiting shows Needs review. Open it.
2. The copy is written by itself (change a line only if you must: it is then kept). Check the photos: on each public photo, cover the plate or mark it not visible.

![](/guides/img/va-fleet-05-listings-desktop-d2672e0a.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 340; address: carmacars.ca/va/listings; pins: 1 54.5 49.1")

3. The listing''s Steps to go live says what is next: 1 Photos, 2 Cover plates, 3 Review, 4 Live on the site, each with its button. The plates are checked by themselves: a plate found is covered (Covered automatically), a photo with none is marked No plate visible, and a photo the check is not sure of stays Plate not checked. **Undo** on a photo takes an automatic decision back. To cover one yourself, press **Cover the plate**: the editor opens under the photo; **Suggest the plate** asks for the box. A photo filed under the wrong shot: **Remove** under it on the Photos card, then take the right one.
4. Drag over a plate to draw a box; drag a box to move it, its corner to resize it.
5. Keep **The CARMA Ontario plate** on a rear plate or **Edit the front plate out** on a front photo (or choose **A CarmaCars plate**, **Pixelation** or **Blur**), then **Save the covered photo**.
6. No plate in the shot? **No plate visible on this photo**.

![](/guides/img/admin-11-plate-editor-phone-95d5afd2.jpg "phone; size: 390 776; pins: 3 52.6 78.9, 4 50.0 43.8, 5 61.5 62.1, 6 43.1 92.3")

> Watch out: The plate check never holds a car back: a photo whose plate is not checked stays private, and goes public by itself once it is covered or marked. The covered photo replaces the public one; the original is kept privately.

## Missing angles and short videos

On a listing, below First photo (Sales: in the Marketplace kit of the car).

1. A required angle with no photo? Fleet and Sales press **Make** and the angle (for example **Make Rear**): the image model makes the view from the car''s photos, within its free daily use. Check it is the same car, then **Approve** or **Reject**.
2. Press **Make a short video** for a 9:16 video of the car''s approved photos with the price and the call to action. Keep the tab in front until it says Saved, then **Download** it or schedule it on your Marketing page (Scheduled posts).

> Watch out: An AI view shows on the site after the real photos, labelled AI view. It is never the cover and never damage or condition evidence. A real photo always replaces it.

## Publish now

Customer service and fleet publish a car themselves; nothing has to be finished first.

1. Open the car from Listings or Field jobs. Its listing says why it is not on the site yet; press **Publish now**. With no rates yet it uses the suggested rates (similar cars, else the class defaults).
2. What is still open (paperwork, details, photos, No VIN yet for a car added by its plate, a possible duplicate) shows as warnings after Publish now and on the car. None of them stops publishing.
3. New cars with their rates usually go on the site by themselves (Publish new cars automatically, on by default). A car taken off the site by staff waits for Publish now.

> Tip: A car not on the fleet insurance policy yet can be requested, offered and paid for, but never handed over until the insurer confirms it. Requests and offers for such a car show a warning.

## Calendar sync with Turo and other platforms

**Cars** > **Calendar sync**: a car listed on Turo or Getaround must never be booked twice.

1. Turo has no calendar link: Turo''s trip emails come in by themselves, find their car by themselves (Turo car number, plate, VIN, year, make, model, trim, colour, what earlier emails taught) and block it with the turnaround. Nothing to set up per car.
2. An email the reader cannot place waits as "Which car is this?": press **Which car is this?** and press the right car (best guesses first). It is remembered for that car''s next emails. If the dates or trip number are missing: **Add as a Turo trip** (choose the car, check the dates) or **Dismiss**. A trip whose email did not come: **Add a Turo trip** on the car.
3. Each Turo trip shows the guest''s name and phone when Turo''s email includes them. Contact a Turo guest only about their trip, never with promotions.
4. Turo cannot read our calendar: under "Block on Turo", block each CarmaCars booking on the car''s Turo calendar, then press **Done on Turo**. Dates that changed or a booking cancelled here show the dates to free on Turo.
5. Getaround, Google Calendar or another platform with a calendar (iCal) link: open **Add a calendar link**, choose the platform, paste it and press **Add the link**. Copy the car''s CarmaCars link for that platform with **Copy** and paste it into the platform''s calendar import.
6. A double booking raises an urgent task for you and an email: move, swap or cancel one trip. A link that stops working raises a task after 3 failed reads: copy it from the platform again.

### Add the photos and readings
A pickup or return recorded with the details later gives Fleet the task **Add the photos and readings for CC-...**. Open the booking and press **Add the check-in (or check-out) photos and readings**: the usual checklist opens without the ready check or the renter''s signature. Take the photos, the odometer, fuel, keys (and cleanliness at a return), sign and save. The task closes by itself; it cannot be closed by hand before.

## Bookings now

**Rentals** > **Bookings** opens on Now for fleet and customer service: the cars out with their renter and due-back countdown, coming back today and tomorrow (overdue first, in red), going out in the next 72 hours with what is ready, the money due in 7 days and the free cars. It refreshes by itself every 30 seconds. A booking listed as **Out (pickup not recorded)** left without a check-in: press **Mark picked up**, then add the photos, km and fuel from the task. A car overdue or due back today has **Returned** (here, on Today and at the top of the booking): give the return time (now, or earlier; the late charges follow it) and the km and fuel if known. The overdue messages stop and the task for the photos is yours. The search above it finds any booking.

### The renter says the car is back

An urgent To do "The renter says the car is back" means the renter pressed **I''ve returned the car** on an overdue booking. Their overdue notices are paused. Open the booking, check the car (place, tracker, the renter''s photos), then press **Confirm** (correct the odometer, fuel or time first if needed; the trip is completed) or **Deny** with the reason (the renter is told and the notices start again).

**Start a listing** takes the VIN from the car: **Scan the barcode** in the door frame or under the windshield, or **Photo of the VIN**.

**Add photos** on a listing takes any number of photos at once, in any order: each is sorted to its shot. A photo that fits no shot goes in with **Extra outside photos** or **Extra inside and detail photos**; drag the extras into their order in the review and press **Save the order**. 10 photos and one outside photo complete the listing. Outside photos are framed big on the studio floor with a shadow under the tyres; a watermark or caption at a photo''s edge is cut off by itself. **Cover the plate** opens with the plate box suggested: check it and save. A car small in the frame, or no model name behind it: press **Frame the outside photos again** (then check the plates again). A bad cut-out (a mirror missing, background left): press **Edit the cut-out**, erase or restore with the brush, move or size the car on the studio, then **Save as a new version**. The version before is kept; if the car did not move, the plate check carries over. Every photo gets a light touch-up by itself; tick **Use original colours** under a photo to make it again without it. Outside photos go in the CarmaCars showroom: a real photographed dealership room when one is stored (the car about 70% of the width, its wheels on the floor, a soft shadow and a faint reflection; no logo on a real wall), else the dark drawn showroom (the logo on the wall, the model''s name behind the car on the cover). A cut-out that is not clean enough is never placed in a room: the real photo is used instead (its plate covered as usual), noted on the photo. A car still on the black studio: press **Apply showroom to this car**; **Listings** > **Apply showroom to every car** does every car. Under a photo, **Redo** makes it again and **Back to the original** puts back the version before. **Marketing photos** on a listing makes copies in other scenes for Marketplace and social posts (choose a scene or **Mix: a different scene on each photo**, then **Make the marketing set**); the website''s photos stay as they are. **First photo** on a listing chooses what shows first on the site and in the Marketplace kit: **Plain car**, **With a model** (the image model''s car-show photo, a fully clothed adult model beside the car) or **Flyer** (the price a day from the live rates, the call to action and the logo on the cover). Switch any time; until the chosen one is made the plain cover shows.
## One screen, many photos (release 28)

**Import photos from a Google Drive link** on a listing adds the photos of a public Drive folder to the car, sorted and processed like Add photos. **Listings** > **Import photos from Drive** reads a whole folder of folders (one per make, then per car), proposes the car for each folder, and imports once you confirm the table. The page follows the import and ends with what was imported, skipped and failed, and why. The same Drive file is never added twice. Customer service can import into a car whose listing is already started; Fleet and Admin can start one.

Check-in and check-out are one screen on the booking page: the time, km, fuel, many photos at once (tag angles if you like) and a note. The renter''s own photos join the same report; each photo shows who took it. On a car''s page, record **Pickup from owner** and **Return to owner** with photos: the owner sees them.

## Repair costs on a car

On a car''s page, **Kickbacks and repairs** lists its repair costs and the kickbacks partners paid on it. **Add a repair cost**: the date, the shop or another vendor, what was done, the amount and tax, who paid (CarmaCars, the owner or the insurer), the claim and a photo or PDF of the receipt.

## When a check stops the pickup or the return (release 33)
On the booking page, **What stops the pickup now** (or the return) lists each check that stops it, in plain words. When the trip must go ahead anyway, press **Ask an Admin to override the pickup** (or the return), give the actual time, the km and fuel if you know them, and why. An Admin gets an alert and approves in one tap; the pickup (or the return) is then recorded with the time you entered, and the booking''s history says who asked and who approved. You can cancel your request while it waits. A trip that happened and was never recorded: **Ask to record a past trip** with both times; once an Admin approves, the booking lands in Returned so the deposit can be settled.

## Incident cards (release 34)
**Cars**, then **Incident cards**, prints the card for the visor or the glovebox: what to do in an accident or a breakdown, our support and roadside numbers, a QR code to report it in the app, and the fleet insurance slip. On a car''s page, **Incident card** prints that car; on the list, **Print all cars** prints every car, two cards to a Letter page with crop marks. Laminate it and put one in each car. The insurance policy on the card is set by an Admin; until it is, the card tells the renter to ask for the slip. No price is ever printed on it.

